{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"set -e\ngit diff --check\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -c 'from tools.orchestrator import allowed_patterns_for, offlimits_changes; from pathlib import Path; changes = offlimits_changes(str(Path.cwd()), allowed_patterns_for(\\\"bench\\\")); print(\\\"Off-limits changes\\\", changes); assert not changes'\ngit status --short\nsed -n '1,120p' implementation_notes.md\"", "aggregated_output": "mkdir -p failed for path /srv/hwebench/homes/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/.config/matplotlib: [Errno 30] Read-only file system: '/srv/hwebench/homes/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/.config'\nMatplotlib created a temporary cache directory at /srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/8e661a23/matplotlib-srxqmmuo because there was an issue with the default path (/srv/hwebench/homes/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/.config/matplotlib); it is highly recommended to set the MPLCONFIGDIR environment variable to a writable directory, in particular to speed up the import of Matplotlib and to better support multiprocessing.\nOff-limits changes []\n M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n# Shared iterative divider\n\n`DIV`, `DIVU`, `REM`, and `REMU` share a restoring divider in `alu.sv`. It consumes five bits per cycle for seven cycles. A single 35-bit register starts with the padded dividend magnitude and shifts in quotient bits. The result transfer applies sign correction to the registered quotient or remainder. Divide by zero selects an explicit result. Signed overflow needs no separate detection logic because the magnitude arithmetic yields quotient bits `0x80000000` and a zero remainder.\n\nEX launches only when the divider is idle and the older EX/MEM entry can advance. It captures the forwarded source operands for RVFI at launch. ID/EX retains the instruction and fetch holds while EX waits. EX/MEM receives a bubble on each unblocked wait cycle so MEM and WB can drain. The completed divide advances through the existing ALU-result forwarding and writeback path. A ready-bus divide takes nine EX cycles. The `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` build captures the existing per-op substitute at launch and uses the same schedule.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed in both the real arithmetic and ALTOPS builds. `alu.sv` includes the guarded core declarations when the alphabetical source glob encounters it first.\n- `formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks, including liveness and all four divide instructions, with zero failures.\n- All 82 cocotb cases passed. The divider tests cover fixed latency, response backpressure, reset during iteration, consecutive requests, and reference arithmetic. The pipeline test checks launch behind a stalled load, consecutive dependent divide and remainder, and one accepting-edge store with correct RVFI operands, results, and order.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random programs with zero-wait and stalled buses. CoreMark completed with all canonical CRCs and the validation message. Real divider arithmetic was checked by the cocotb reference vectors and ISS co-simulation.\n\n## Gowin and CoreMark\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 42.639, 45.881, and 45.881 MHz. The median was **45.881 MHz**, up from 5.442 MHz. The option-0 worst setup path ran from the register file through ID, EX, and the ALU to data memory. Its reported arrival time was **28.747 ns across 18 logic cells**, down from 199.837 ns across 156 cells.\n\nWith both standard bus stalls enabled, the start and stop markers were at cycles 15,801 and 4,507,286. The **4,491,485 measured cycles** matched a fresh simulation of the baseline. The two `DIVU` retirements fell outside the measured interval. The first, at PC `0x12b8`, moved from cycle 168 to 176. The measured fitness was **102.15 CoreMark iterations/s**, about 8.43 times the baseline at the same cycle count.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
