{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_157","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"set -e\ngit diff --check\ndiff -qr cores/bench/rtl \\\"/srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/7f9fcc67/bench-repair-b.Oy40Wbuj/cores/bench/rtl\\\"\ncmp cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py \\\"/srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/7f9fcc67/bench-repair-b.Oy40Wbuj/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\\\"\ngit status --short\nsed -n '1,100p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n# Apply repair at the fetch FIFO state boundary\n\n- Normal enqueue uses imem readiness, space in the pre-edge FIFO, and exact replay validation. Normal dequeue uses hazard eligibility and the last lane of the nonempty head. These credits drive the one-hot occupancy update. A full FIFO declines a normal response even on a pop.\n- Repair overrides the FIFO state update, selects slot zero and its bus word, and seeds occupancy directly from imem readiness. A stalled corrected request leaves the FIFO empty and retries the corrected PC. Reset selects an empty FIFO.\n- The replay check registers whether an accepted guess will be at the head. This holds when the FIFO was empty or its sole old slot popped. The registered guess qualifies the saved bit. The full tag and instruction word still determine exact validation, and the checked-slot index locates the replay lane mask write.\n- Divider wait is independent of repair. The existing flush-first ID/EX valid update clears younger work even when divider wait is high. Repair gates divider launch and result acceptance, retains the resolver in EX/MEM, and holds MEM/WB.\n- A rejected bus response may write payload RAM at the unclaimed tail. Only an accepted credit makes the slot visible. The repaired slot starts with a cleared replay lane mask and the pending validation is discarded.\n- Added pipeline coverage for an exact replay hit behind older queued words when a divide releases issue.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint and all six cocotb runners passed. Cosim passed selftest and all three random programs with and without stalls. The stalled CoreMark run produced the canonical CRCs in 3,750,582 marker cycles.\n- The local single-channel `formal/run_all.sh` suite generated 53 checks. As of the latest check, 8 passed, including liveness, retirement uniqueness, illegal-instruction handling, and DIV/DIVU in ALTOPS mode. The remaining checks were pending, with zero failures and no counterexample observed.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 90.460, 99.606, and 99.606 MHz. The median corresponds to 265.57 CoreMark iterations/s and falls short of the 106.214 MHz acceptance boundary. The longest paths in the median placements run from the issue word to ID result-lane selection and through EX forwarding. A fresh build of the champion reproduced 101.544 MHz on option 1.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
