{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_125","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'async def (divide_forwarding_with_stalled_store|load_use_stalls|forwarding_load_result_through_store_stall|jalr_misalignment_carry_suppresses_link|jalr_repair_forwards_link_to_divide|repair_over_pending_alias_and_wrong_path_divide)' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py && git diff --stat && cat implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"334:async def forwarding_load_result_through_store_stall(dut, rs2):\n373:async def load_use_stalls(dut, stall_cycles):\n459:async def divide_forwarding_with_stalled_store(dut):\n663:async def jalr_repair_forwards_link_to_divide(dut, correction_wait):\n695:async def jalr_misalignment_carry_suppresses_link(dut, nops_before_jump):\n914:async def repair_over_pending_alias_and_wrong_path_divide(dut, correction_wait):\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  9 +++++----\n cores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv    |  3 ++-\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv       |  9 ++++-----\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 4 files changed, 43 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)\n# Execute bypass qualification at capture\n\n- EX producer eligibility uses registered ID/EX validity and the trap-adjusted destination write control. The load-use interlock holds the dependent fetch word for the MEM/WB path. A trapping jump leaves the older producer eligible.\n- Raw divide wait holds ID independently of repair. Repair clears ID/EX validity before the hold and preserves the EX/MEM resolver and MEM/WB forwarding word. Divider launch and result consumption still require EX to advance.\n- IF computes normal issue from the raw hazards. Repair selects slot zero, seeds occupancy from instruction memory readiness, and selects the bus lane before any subsequent replay advance.\n- Added a JALR repair test with a held store, a wrong-path divide and store, and a corrected divide that consumes the link. The test exercises both immediate and stalled correction responses and checks that the next store consumes the divide result on the adjacent retirement cycle.\n\n## Local verification and timing\n\n- Verilator lint passed. The cocotb suite and five-ELF cosimulation passed for the capture changes. Stalled CoreMark reproduced 3,750,582 marker cycles and the canonical CRCs.\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 measured 96.281, 102.627, and 102.627 MHz. The median projects to 273.63 iterations/s and falls below the 106.215 MHz acceptance threshold. The wide-divider recurrence limited timing, with forwarding into the shared integer result lane close behind.\n- The unchanged single-retirement formal suite is running in a scratch copy of the framework.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
