{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; rows=map(json.loads,Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines()); [print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"seeds\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\")},indent=2)) for r in rows if r.get(\\\"round_id\\\")==11]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r11s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Qualify execute bypass at the pipeline capture boundary\",\n  \"seeds\": [\n    96.281,\n    102.627,\n    102.627\n  ],\n  \"cycles\": 3750582,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/wide_dividend_quotient_q_20_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/wide_remainder_q_28_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -5.386,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 15.681,\n    \"logic_cells\": 42,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"# Execute bypass qualification at capture\\n\\n- EX producer eligibility uses registered ID/EX validity and the trap-adjusted destination write control. The load-use interlock holds the dependent fetch word for the MEM/WB path. A trapping jump leaves the older producer eligible.\\n- Raw divide wait holds ID independently of repair. Repair clears ID/EX validity before the hold and preserves the EX/MEM resolver and MEM/WB forwarding word. Divider launch and result consumption still require EX to advance.\\n- IF computes normal issue from the raw hazards. Repair selects slot zero, seeds occupancy from instruction memory readiness, and selects the bus lane before any subsequent replay advance.\\n- Added a JALR repair test with a held store, a wrong-path divide and store, and a corrected divide that consumes the link. The test exercises both immediate and stalled correction responses and checks that the next store consumes the divide result on the adjacent retirement cycle.\\n- Used the existing FIFO response and forwarding lanes. A broader fetch response split and the tested operand-decode and divider-lane changes yielded lower placement results.\\n\\n## Local verification and timing\\n\\n- Verilator lint, six cocotb runners, and five-ELF cosimulation passed. The directed pipeline tests covered the repaired JALR, wrong-path divide, adjacent divide consumers, held data memory responses, and forwarding from an older producer after a trapping jump. Stalled CoreMark reproduced 3,750,582 marker cycles and the canonical CRCs.\\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 measured 96.281, 102.627, and 102.627 MHz. The median projects to 273.63 iterations/s and falls below the 106.215 MHz acceptance threshold. The wide-divider recurrence limited timing, with forwarding into the shared integer result lane close behind.\\n- Local formal remained incomplete within the implementation time budget. The single-retirement suite ran in a scratch copy of the framework. Eleven of 53 checks passed, including liveness, unique retirement order, illegal instructions, JALR, DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. The remaining solvers were pending with zero failures or counterexamples reported.\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r11s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Resolve load-fed branches with registered comparison groups\",\n  \"seeds\": [\n    98.92,\n    101.716,\n    101.716\n  ],\n  \"cycles\": 3621253,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/wide_dividend_quotient_q_21_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/wide_remainder_q_2_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -5.109,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 15.403,\n    \"logic_cells\": 42,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r11s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Predict the direct transfer at the end of a replay prefix\",\n  \"seeds\": [\n    93.059,\n    92.042,\n    92.042\n  ],\n  \"cycles\": 3679487,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/repair_direct_q_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_default_10_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -5.746,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 16.04,\n    \"logic_cells\": 8,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_id\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
