{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_132","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat implementation_notes.md && rg -n '\"'^SBY.+(failed assertion|DONE '\"\\\\(FAIL|DONE \\\\(ERROR)' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR\"/bench-formal.Ni31lkv8/gate.log'","aggregated_output":"# Adjacent load forwarding\n\nDecode prequalifies BEQ/BNE and loads with offsets 0, 1, or 2 from the registered issue word. The accepted pair requires an `rs1` dependency on a nonzero load destination, and the address path requires an LW producer. The ID/EX payload records the pair, the raw `rs2` match, and the two offset bits. Other raw source matches retain the load-use interlock.\n\nThe branch path checks the active raw response bytes and verifies extension in parallel. The independent operand can use the registered default or MEM/WB forwarding. Equality, ordered branches, and load-fed equality all feed the same two EX/MEM comparison registers. The edge also captures the prediction-qualified repair enables and the correction PC pair for direct control transfers. The MEM stage resolves the polarity for repair, training, and retirement. Predictor word capture uses the memory stall directly because every repairing instruction terminates a prefix. The resolver retains its comparison and next PC through the repair hold.\n\nThe address path adds the short offset with prefix reductions and XOR, then captures the full byte address at the regular EX/MEM edge. Data stalls hold both instructions. Misaligned producers provide no load response, so the consumer uses its ordinary forwarded operands. Misaligned consumers follow the usual trap and bus-mask logic. Extended response values reach RVFI independently of the timed branch and address paths, including when a load immediate aliases the producer's destination in the raw `rs2` field.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed. All six cocotb runners passed. Directed cases check exact retirement order and operands, byte lanes and extension, carry and wraparound, held responses with invalid data, trapped pairs, and dependencies that retain the interlock. Existing predictor tests check taken and untaken repairs and suppression of younger effects.\n- Five-ELF cosim passed, including ISS trace comparisons with and without stalls and stalled CoreMark CRC validation. The canonical run retired the benchmark in 3,565,123 marker cycles, saving 185,459 cycles from the champion.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
