{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_152","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --name-only; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard; git diff --check; nl -ba cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n     1\t# Adjacent load consumers\n     2\t\n     3\tIF predecodes aligned BEQ and BNE instructions and legal loads with offsets 0–2. The eligibility bits advance with the instruction through bus acceptance, replay installation, the FIFO, and the issue mirror. ID admits a pair when the older load writes the consumer's first source. Pointer loads additionally require an LW producer. The existing forwarding selections supply the fallback after a load alignment trap.\n     4\t\n     5\tEX checks the selected raw lane and the extension in parallel for byte and halfword loads. Word comparisons use two 16-bit predicates. EX/MEM retains both predicates and the branch polarity through repair. The separate request chooses the existing direct or fall-through PC pair. Normal branches and jumps use the existing resolver. Repair takes priority over FIFO and ID valid updates and qualifies divider issue and completion.\n     6\t\n     7\tThe address path selects the raw word or the ordinary effective address in parallel with the short-offset carry calculation. The prefix carries only modify the selected raw word. This keeps dmem driven by the existing EX/MEM address register and reduces delay through the RAM-to-address path. A stalled response holds the pair, and a misaligned producer selects the ordinary address. The normal MEM alignment and bus-mask checks run on the consumer. RVFI reports the complete load result for each matching source, including a load immediate's raw second-source field.\n     8\t\n     9\tReplay training advances from MEM/WB. Reset and FENCE.I clear pending training. The four replay scenarios allow an extra training cycle and retain their exact retirement, prediction, and accepted bus assertions. Added cases cover stalls with invalid response data, both branch polarities and correction directions, trapped-producer fallback, dependent pointer loads through replay, and exact RVFI operands.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Local verification\n    12\t\n    13\tThe first formal run reported 52 passes and a `pc_fwd_ch0` failure. Its witness showed the packed-struct fetch arrays returning zero for queued bus and replay words under Yosys. Moved the fetch storage to plain vectors, which also restored Gowin distributed RAM inference. The next formal run passed the failing forward-PC check. The gate for the selected RTL is running in a scratch copy of the formal framework.\n    14\t\n    15\tGowin placements 0, 1, and 2 measured 84.831, 101.148, and 101.148 MHz. All inferred five BSRAMs. The median clears the 101.002 MHz floor at 3,566,506 marker cycles and projects to 283.61 CoreMark iterations/s, up 4.75% from the champion. The median is limited by ordinary forwarded branch resolution, with the raw-load comparison close behind. The option 0 critical path remains the data RAM address feedback.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
