{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\ngit diff --check\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom os import environ\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import parse_reports\nroot = Path(environ['TMPDIR']) / 'replay-timing-final'\nfor d in sorted(root.glob('gowin_p?')):\n    p = parse_reports(d)\n    print(d.name, p['fmax_mhz'], p['logic'], p['regs'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,160p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\ngit diff --check\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom os import environ\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import parse_reports\nroot = Path(environ['TMPDIR']) / 'replay-timing-final'\nfor d in sorted(root.glob('gowin_p?')):\n    p = parse_reports(d)\n    print(d.name, p['fmax_mhz'], p['logic'], p['regs'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Register partial matches for exact fetch replay validation\n\nThe fetch stage registers twelve four-bit equality results in place of two 45-bit identities. The operands contain the cursor or stored full tag and all 32 instruction bits, with three high zero bits filling the last group. Every clock samples the predicates alongside the checked slot and last-lane mask. A simultaneous table write leaves validation and replay metadata sampling the same pre-edge row.\n\nIn the following cycle, the registered guess qualifies the AND of the twelve predicates. The existing rejection, credit, lane and repair logic consumes this result at the original validation boundary. Reset and FENCE.I still clear speculative state through the existing control paths.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint and all six cocotb runners passed. The pipeline suite covered short-tag aliases, changed source instructions, a stalled speculative resume, older repair with ready and stalled correction responses, and FENCE.I.\n- A two-step Yosys SAT equivalence check proved all 9,310 matched fetch-stage points against the original RTL, including the checked hit, rejection and FIFO occupancy.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the ISS in both bus modes. Stalled CoreMark validated all five CRCs and completed ten iterations in 3,564,868 marker cycles.\n- The single-channel `formal/run_all.sh` suite is running with the existing configuration.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\nPlacement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 96.643, 106.724 and 106.724 MHz. The build used 2,324 registers and 7,212 LUT4s. The median placements were limited by execute forwarding into the ALU result register. The replay comparison to FIFO occupancy was absent from their 25 worst setup paths.\n\nThe 106.724 MHz median gives 299.38 CoreMark iterations/s at the measured cycle count, below the 299.41 acceptance cutoff. Factoring rejection separately and expressing each four-bit equality as two two-bit equalities each lowered the median Fmax, so the implementation uses the proposed four-bit comparisons and the existing rejection expression.\ngowin_p0 96.643 7212 2324\ngowin_p1 106.724 7212 2324\ngowin_p2 106.724 7212 2324\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
