{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_159","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git diff --stat; git diff --numstat; rg -n -m1 'RISC.*ALT' formal/checks_si.cfg; rg -c 'DONE \\\\(PASS' \\\"\"'$TMPDIR/bench-shift-native-formal.log\"; tail -2 \"$TMPDIR/bench-shift-native-timing.log\"; date -u'","aggregated_output":"# Register shifts in a separate execute result bank\n\nID/EX captures the left, right, and arithmetic shift enables from the validated ALU opcode. Holds retain the enables, and reset or a decode bubble clears them. EX/MEM captures a shift word and a nonshift word on the same advancing edge. Each inactive bank supplies zero, including during bubbles and while a divide is pending. Both words use the existing `other` result tag in EX forwarding and MEM writeback.\n\nEach EX operand ORs four terms in a final LUT4. ADD/SUB and multiply low/high each form a LUT4 term. The tagged bank merge and the masked MEM/WB word plus its prequalified ID/EX default each form a LUT3 term. Forwarding eligibility, branch and ALU comparisons, direct target fetch, and the load-use interlock retain the champion's logic.\n\nThe standalone ALU still decodes shifts from its opcode and exposes its combined result. With unrestricted optimization, Gowin shared the untagged merge across operands and added a third LUT on a measured shift-data path. The `operand_forward` module therefore uses Gowin LUT primitives and uses the same INIT truth tables for Verilator and Yosys.\n\nThe new pipeline tests check every shift amount for both source signs and both instruction forms. They check exact RVFI sources and back-to-back retirement for adjacent consumers, including a shift-to-shift dependency. Directed store holds exercise both directions of forwarding between the shift and nonshift banks. A stalled load followed by an immediate shift checks that the load-use interlock still inserts one bubble.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- The full-core Verilator lint command passed without warnings. All six cocotb runners passed.\n- The unmodified cosim gate passed for all five ELFs. The four full-trace ELFs matched the ISS both with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed its CRC checks.\n- Exhaustive evaluation of each LUT INIT matched its stated Boolean function.\n cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv            |  42 +++++++++++-----\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |   8 +++\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  75 +++++++++++++++-------------\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       |   8 +++\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv      |   2 +-\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 101 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 6 files changed, 188 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)\n29\t13\tcores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n8\t0\tcores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n41\t34\tcores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n8\t0\tcores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n1\t1\tcores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n101\t0\tcores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n26:# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n25\nSat Nov 21 00:57:09 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
