{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\"):\n    d=json.loads(line)\n    if d.get(\\\"id\\\") == \\\"hyp-20261121-001-r8s0\\\":\n        h=d.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\") or {}\n        print(d.keys())\n        print(str(h)[:14000])\n        print(str(d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))[:5000])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n{'motivation': \"The bench champion scores 251.02 CoreMark iter/s at 104.134 MHz over 4,148,503 marker cycles. In the median-setting Gowin placements, execute forwarding into the shared integer result was within 0.005 ns of the longest setup path. The shifter currently feeds result selection along with bitwise, PC-relative, link, and divide terms. Removing those terms from the shifter's register input targets that path without adding a dependency cycle.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Split the current EX/MEM other-result word into two zero-masked banks. One bank captures SLL, SRL, and SRA using registered ID/EX shift enables. The second bank captures the remaining integer and special results. Use one shared other-result tag for both banks. On every advancing edge, a bank supplies zero when its operation class is inactive. A shift still forwards to the immediately following instruction.\\n\\nPreserve two LUT4 levels per forwarded operand. Combine the two registered banks and their shared tag in one LUT3. Combine the masked MEM/WB word and the prequalified ID/EX default in another LUT3. The ADD/SUB pair and multiply-low/high pair each occupy one LUT4. Reduce those four terms in a final LUT4. MEM merges the two banks under the same tag for writeback.\\n\\nPreserve direct target fetch, exact RVFI source values, the existing load-use interlock, and stall-aligned forwarding. Exercise adjacent shift consumers, all shift amounts and signedness, and dmem holds across bank changes. A preliminary prototype that also changed branch and compare logic reached 97.008 MHz. Isolate the bank split on the champion's current comparator and one-hot forwarding controls. With the same cycle count, acceptance requires a median above approximately 108.93 MHz. A 110 MHz median would yield about 265.16 iter/s. The timing target is unverified and the divide and branch paths may cap the median after the split. Run the unmodified formal and cosim gates and measure all three Gowin placements.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/core_pkg.sv', 'description': 'Add the registered shift bank and ID/EX shift enables. Keep one forwarding tag for both other-result banks.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Predecode left, right, and arithmetic-right shift enables from validated decoder outputs. Capture them with the current ID/EX hold and flush rules.'}, {'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Expose separate shift and nonshift outputs for EX while preserving the exact combinational ALU results and standalone test behavior.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register separately masked shift and nonshift results and group the forwarding terms into four first-level LUT functions.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'OR the two registered other-result banks under their shared writeback select.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Cover adjacent shift dependencies, shift signedness and distances, and forwarding across stalled cycles that separate producers from their consumers.'}]}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
