{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '240,320p' formal/run_all.sh && tail -c 6500 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && ls -l bench/programs/*.elf\"", "aggregated_output": "    first=\"${FAILED[0]}\"\n    if [ -f \"$first/logfile.txt\" ]; then\n        echo \"\"\n        echo \"--- $first/logfile.txt (last 30 lines) ---\"\n        tail -30 \"$first/logfile.txt\"\n    fi\n    echo \"\"\n    echo \"Full run log: $LOG\"\n    echo \"Per-check logs in: $CORE_DIR/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\"\nfi\n[ $FAIL -eq 0 ]\nset\\nand PC+offset+1. In parallel compute the high 15 bits with carry-in\\nzero and with carry-in one. Capture these partial sums with the decoded\\nword on the normal ID/EX edge. EX selects each high half with its saved\\ncarry and uses the assembled target and successor for repair. AUIPC\\nuses the same assembled sum for its writeback result. This cuts the\\nfull-width carry path into EX/MEM, including the measured PC-to-AUIPC\\nresult path, without adding a repair cycle. Preserve the full-width\\narchitectural PC, alignment checks, JALR and FENCE.I priority, and the\\nexisting trap, bus, and single-channel RVFI contracts.\\n\\nA scratch target-only implementation with independent repair credits\\ncompleted canonical CoreMark in 3,704,180 marker cycles with all five\\nCRCs and the validation banner. It measured 100.821 MHz in placement\\noption 1, where the longest path ran from the ID/EX PC through the\\nPC-relative adder to EX/MEM result.other. The split PC adder still\\nneeds timing measurements. At this cycle count the acceptance floor\\nof 283.194 iterations/s requires a median above\\n104.900 MHz. Target 105.5 MHz, or 284.81 iterations/s. Measure all\\nthree placements and run the existing formal and cosim gates.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a predictor fill q