{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines()]; print(len(rows)); print(str(rows[-1])[:4200])'\"", "aggregated_output": "43\n{'id': 'hyp-20261121-003-r14s2', 'title': 'Replay either predicted successor of a conditional branch', 'category': 'predictor', 'motivation': 'The bench champion takes 3,564,868 marker cycles at 102.041 MHz.\\nA reproduced run counted 275,041 cycles with issue ready and the fetch\\nFIFO empty, 235,163 fall-through conditional branches, and 74,124\\nB/JAL repairs. The current predictor supplies up to four words after\\ntaken transfers. Making fall-through branches replay entry points\\nincreases the opportunities to supply instructions during imem stalls.\\nThe same predictor can anticipate taken transfers whose target starts\\nwith another branch, even when it has no words to replay.\\n', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The bench champion takes 3,564,868 marker cycles at 102.041 MHz.\\nA reproduced run counted 275,041 cycles with issue ready and the fetch\\nFIFO empty, 235,163 fall-through conditional branches, and 74,124\\nB/JAL repairs. The current predictor supplies up to four words after\\ntaken transfers. Making fall-through branches replay entry points\\nincreases the opportunities to supply instructions during imem stalls.\\nThe same predictor can anticipate taken transfers whose target starts\\nwith another branch, even when it has no words to replay.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Give each of 128 direct-mapped rows a two-bit conditional direction\\ncounter and one sequential packet of up to eight words for the\\ncurrently favored successor. Index with PC[8:2] XOR PC[15:9] and\\nretain PC[19:9] for exact validation within the instruction window.\\nA 32-row trial lost the cycle savings when fall-through entries\\ndisplaced taken entries. The larger table reduces these conflicts.\\nStart collection from either resolved successor of a legal B or\\nfrom the target of a legal JAL in the surviving EX/MEM advance\\nstream. End before any control transfer, discontinuity, trap, or\\ninstruction-window boundary. A direct transfer can finish one packet\\nand start another on the same advance. A taken transfer with an\\nempty packet installs a target-o\n…[1132 of 4204 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4995ec771c0bb376]…\nistered PC. Form the two PC successors in parallel. Register\\nthe narrow forecast and the current response-rejection bit separately\\nso full identity validation stays out of the next forecast register's\\ninput path. Mask the forecast before steering or making a new\\nvalidation attempt if its response was rejected.\\n\\nSnapshot the first predecoded replay word with the accepted source.\\nRead later lanes from synchronous block RAM on that same edge and\\ncopy them to the corresponding FIFO slot on exact validation. The\\nfirst word can enter the issue register while the later words are\\ncaptured. Reject a same-row payload read and write collision at\\nvalidation before using any of the sampled payload. Keep validated\\ndirection separate from the last-lane mask. A fall-through packet\\nholds its slot through the last lane and predicts the source\\nnot taken. A target-only hit predicts taken and pops on source\\nissue. An alias discards the younger speculative response and\\nrestores fetching at the source PC+4.\\n\\nKeep\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
