{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_44", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '101\\\\.544|270\\\\.74' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | tail -n 2\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r9s2\", \"title\": \"Steer fetch early and validate target replay alongside decode\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"Single-word target replay reduced stalled CoreMark from 4,148,503 to\\n3,819,059 marker cycles. Six-word replay saved another 64,323 cycles\\nand routed at 84.404 MHz. Gowin reported the critical path from the\\nfetch cursor through the replay lookup and hit logic into the active\\npacket's prediction register. Separate early cursor steering from\\nexact validation and overlap validation with decode to preserve\\nfetch throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Single-word target replay reduced stalled CoreMark from 4,148,503 to\\n3,819,059 marker cycles. Six-word replay saved another 64,323 cycles\\nand routed at 84.404 MHz. Gowin reported the critical path from the\\nfetch cursor through the replay lookup and hit logic into the active\\npacket's prediction register. Separate early cursor steering from\\nexact validation and overlap validation with decode to preserve\\nfetch throughput.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Index a 32-entry direct-mapped predictor with fetch PC[6:2].\\nThe early steering decision uses a valid bit, a taken forecast\\nfrom the two-bit counter, a four-bit partial PC tag PC[10:7],\\nand a B/JAL opcode check on the accepted word. In parallel, read\\nthe saved resume PC. Capture it and the fall-through PC in\\nseparate cursor banks. The early decision drives a registered bank\\nselector so the next imem request can start after the prefix.\\nKeep the fast forecast and short tag in a narrow array separate\\nfrom the full tag, exact source instruction, and replay payload.\\n\\nWrite the bus word, raw replay words, and target PC into separate\\nflat lanes of a four-slot FIFO at fetch acceptance. Store unreset\\npayloads and reset the validity state. Use registered occupancy for\\ncredits and a registered lane index for issue. Latch the raw full\\ntag, source signature, length, and guess with the response's slot\\nindex. On the following cycle validate the registered full tag and\\nexact s\n…[9126 of 12198 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e9668b3cecc6cd60]…\nnterexample.\\n- Verilator lint and all six pytest runners passed. The pipeline runner passed all 33 scenarios. Cosimulation passed selftest and all three random programs with and without bus stalls, plus canonical stalled CoreMark.\\n- Canonical stalled CoreMark validated all five CRCs and completed 10 iterations in 3,750,582 marker cycles. Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 95.873, 101.544, and 101.544 MHz. The median yielded 270.74 iterations/s against the 262.57 iterations/s floor. The option 0 critical path starts in the registered JALR repair control and ends in FIFO occupancy.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T02:33:29.845565Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 9, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r9s2 (improvement, +7.86%): Registering fetch steering from a short PC tag and direction counter let full-tag and exact-instruction replay validation overlap decode, removing the validation logic from the fetch feedback path and yielding a 101.544 MHz median Gowin Fmax at 3,750,582 stalled CoreMark cycles.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
