{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_161","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; date -Is; rg 'DONE \\\\(' formal/last_run-wXrG2JXRu.log | tail -12; sed -n '1,36p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"2026-11-21T11:36:51+01:00\nSBY 11:35:37 [causal_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY 11:35:37 [ill_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY 11:35:42 [pc_bwd_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY 11:35:48 [liveness_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nSBY 11:35:57 [unique_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\n# Conditional successor replay\n\nThe predictor now has 128 direct-mapped rows indexed by `PC[8:2] ^ PC[15:9]`. The surviving EX/MEM stream supplies the resolved successor of each legal branch or JAL and up to eight consecutive words. Control transfers, traps, discontinuities, and the instruction-window boundary end collection. The collector leaves the last word of the window on the bus path so the saved resume PC stays in range. A taken observation can install a target-only row, and an empty fall-through observation can train a matching row's counter.\n\nTraining registers the hash, samples the row, then decides what to publish. It skips a sample while an older update owns the same row. Matching outcomes refresh the packet when the source instruction changes or the observed prefix grows. This avoids rewriting identical payloads during hot loops. The collector releases one lane per advance, so each training stage captures just the next lane that could be overwritten before publication.\n\nFetch reads the two short-tag forecasts in parallel and registers the forecast separately from response rejection. A full source check and same-row payload write check govern validation. The first predecoded word is captured from LUT RAM with the source, and block RAM supplies identity metadata and the remaining seven words. The table encodes packet length in four bits and validation expands it into a last-lane mask. The queue tracks direction independently. Two issue-word registers let the load-use interlock control a narrow selector. EX still resolves the architectural path and squashes younger work. Reset and FENCE.I clear row validity and in-flight training.\n\nDirected tests cover the hashed aliases and changed instructions, stalled eight-word fall-through replay, reversals with a younger store, empty fall-through training, target-only chaining, same-row updates and collisions, FENCE.I, and full-width links at the instruction-window boundary.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint, all six cocotb runners, and single-channel co-simulation passed. Co-simulation covered selftest, three random traces, and CoreMark. The canonical stalled CoreMark run completed 10 iterations in 3,414,350 marker cycles, 150,518 fewer than the champion. The UART banner and all five canonical CRCs matched, with `oob=false`.\n- `formal/run_all.sh` was run with the single-channel wrapper. The complete formal gate remains unverified within the local time budget. No counterexample was reported.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 93.550, 96.111, and 96.111 MHz. The median corresponds to 281.49 iterations/s and missed the 103 MHz target. Option 0 used 7,901 LUT4, 2,768 registers, and 17 block RAMs. The worst paths run from the source-instruction block RAM through exact validation to the fetch occupancy register.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
