lots and issue mirror. One bit marks BEQ/BNE with an aligned target.\n  The other marks a legal load with an offset of 0, 1 or 2. Admit the\n  adjacent consumer when its rs1 matches the older load's nonzero\n  destination. Require an LW producer for the address case. Factor the\n  hazard as a first-source hit that needs the bubble, or a second-source\n  hit without a\n…[3405 of 6477 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:04953fd4baace4f7]…\nallbacks.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Skip the load-use interlock for eligible pairs while preserving data holds and repair priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Route load-pair eligibility, memory data and producer qualification. Register replay training alongside MEM/WB and preserve fence invalidation.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the aligned load response qualification and extended word for forwarding and RVFI.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture dedicated load-fed equality and repair predicates, preserve ordinary branch resolution, and select the short-offset load address before the existing address register.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Account for the extra training cycle in the four replay scenarios while exercising the same predictions and repairs. Check held load responses, both equality outcomes and correction directions, misaligned producer fallback, adjacent pointer loads, and exact raw RVFI operands.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
