{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"tail -3 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c 1-1600 && git log -1 --format='%B'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r10s1\", \"title\": \"Resolve load-dependent equality branches after load writeback capture\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 270.74 CoreMark iterations/s at 101.544 MHz\\nand 3,750,582 marker cycles. The canonical stalled retirement trace\\ncontains 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions immediately after a load whose\\nnonzero destination they read. They occupy a load-use bubble today.\\nA direct data-RAM-to-EX comparator saved 129,454 marker cycles in a\\nscratch run, but the added RAM-to-repair path limited median Gowin\\nFmax to 65.652 MHz. Resolving these branches from registered load\\ndata can recover the issue slots while preserving a register boundary\\nat the memory response.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 270.74 CoreMark iterations/s at 101.544 MHz\\nand 3,750,582 marker cycles. The canonical stalled retirement trace\\ncontains 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions immediately after a load whose\\nnonzero destination they read. They occupy a load-use bubble today.\\nA direct data-RAM-to-EX comparator saved 129,454 marker cycles in a\\nscratch run, but the added RAM-to-repair path limited median Gowin\\nFmax to 65.652 MHz. Resolving these branches from registered load\\ndata can recover the issue slots while preserving a register boundary\\nat the memory response.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Classify a legal BEQ or BNE using the destination of the current\\nvalid EX load as a deferred branch. Register the two source matches\\nin ID/EX and admit the branch without the normal load-use bubble.\\nKeep that bubble for other consum\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r10s2\", \"title\": \"Separate direct prediction from replay packet completion\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 270.74 iterations/s at 101.544 MHz over\\n3,750,582 stalled CoreMark marker cycles. The predictor can install a\\ntaken entry only when it collects a replay word. This leaves a hot B\\nor JAL unpredicted when its target starts with another control transfer.\\nThe champion's marker w\n…[1771 of 4843 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bff236be66b751bd]…\n\": \"The bench champion scores 270.74 iterations/s at 101.544 MHz over\\n3,750,582 stalled CoreMark marker cycles. Its registered repair feeds\\nEX validity and divider wait, then ID operand defaults and fetch\\noccupancy. ID consumes the EX bypass selects only when its new\\ninstruction survives the edge. Repair already clears that validity,\\nand an incomplete divide holds ID/EX, so neither condition needs to\\npass through the bypass producer match.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Compute the EX producer match from registered ID/EX validity, validated\\ndestination write control, and the current jump alignment result.\\nSelect the delayed MEM/WB bypass for loads and let an older eligible\\nproducer supply the operand when a younger jump traps. Let the younger\\nconsumer register operand selections under the ID capture and flush\\nrules. In the repair cycle the consumer is invalidated regardless of\\nthe match. While a divide is incomplete the consumer holds its prior\\noperands. At completion\nlog: hyp-20261121-001-r11s0 regression\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
