{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nkeys = ('id', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'fmax_mhz', 'cycles', 'seeds', 'critical_path', 'implementation_notes', 'lesson')\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    record = json.loads(line)\n    if record.get('id') in {'hyp-20261121-002-r13s1', 'hyp-20261121-001-r12s0'}:\n        print(json.dumps({key: record.get(key) for key in keys}, indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nkeys = ('id', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'fmax_mhz', 'cycles', 'seeds', 'critical_path', 'implementation_notes', 'lesson')\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    record = json.loads(line)\n    if record.get('id') in {'hyp-20261121-002-r13s1', 'hyp-20261121-001-r12s0'}:\n        print(json.dumps({key: record.get(key) for key in keys}, indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r12s0\",\n  \"outcome\": \"regression\",\n  \"fitness\": 277.47,\n  \"delta_pct\": 2.49,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 98.923,\n  \"cycles\": 3565123,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    95.642,\n    98.923,\n    98.923\n  ],\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_if/resume_q_4_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/guess_q_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -5.456,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 15.75,\n    \"logic_cells\": 10,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"# Adjacent load forwarding\\n\\nDecode prequalifies BEQ/BNE and loads with offsets 0, 1, or 2 from the registered issue word. The accepted pair requires an `rs1` dependency on a nonzero load destination, and the address path requires an LW producer. The ID/EX payload records the pair, the raw `rs2` match, and the two offset bits. Other raw source matches retain the load-use interlock.\\n\\nThe branch path checks the active raw response bytes and verifies extension in parallel. The independent operand can use the registered default or MEM/WB forwarding. Equality, ordered branches, and load-fed equality all feed the same two EX/MEM comparison registers. The edge also captures the prediction-qualified repair enables and correction PC pair for direct control transfers. MEM completes the comparison and applies its polarity for repair, training, and retirement. The resolver retains its comparison and next PC through the repair hold.\\n\\nThe address path adds the short offset with prefix reductions and XOR, then captures the full byte address at the regular EX/MEM edge. Data stalls hold both instructions. Misaligned producers provide no load response, so the consumer uses its ordinary forwarded operands. Misaligned consumers follow the usual trap and bus-mask logic. Extended response values reach RVFI independently of the timed branch and address paths, including when a load immediate aliases the producer's destination in the raw `rs2` field.\\n\\n## Local verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint and all 50 directed pipeline cases passed on the retained RTL. The tests check exact retire\n…[1158 of 4230 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:19be9c4026a71880]…\ns. Options 1 and 2 were limited by JALR correction into fetch at 10.109 ns, with branch-to-training at 10.086 ns. The data RAM feedback into the effective-address register did not appear among the reported top 25 setup paths for any option.\\n\\nA trial with unconditional repairs folded into the comparison controls and localized predictor word capture measured 92.556, 96.756, and 96.756 MHz. A further trial moved the JALR successor into EX to shorten its fetch path. Its option 0 measured 91.100 MHz and was limited by ordinary EX operand forwarding into the result lane. Its other reports were pending at the end of the local run.\\n\",\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r12s0 (regression, +2.49%): With prefix carries for offsets 0\\u20132, LW-to-load forwarding left RAM-to-address feedback outside the top 25 setup paths, with JALR correction into fetch capping median Gowin Fmax at 98.923 MHz, below the 100.962 MHz needed to win after the address and BEQ/BNE bypasses saved 185,459 stalled CoreMark cycles.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
