r LUT3. The ADD/SUB pair and multiply-low/high pair each occupy one LUT4. Reduce those four terms in a final LUT4. MEM merges the two banks under the same tag for writeback.\\n\\nPreserve direct target fetch, exact RVFI source values, the existing load-use interlock, and stall-aligned forwarding. Exercise adjacent shift consumers, all sh\n…[2850 of 5922 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:43e6176724d07535]…\n\": 1694.8, \"fmax_mhz\": 90.243, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4148503, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 4459, \"ff\": 1381, \"seeds\": [89.963, 90.243, 90.243], \"perturbations\": [[0, 89.963, 14], [1, 90.243, 14], [2, 90.243, 14]], \"lutram\": 32, \"bsram\": 5, \"dsp\": 4, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_default_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.result.other_0_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.116, \"arrival_ns\": 16.41, \"logic_cells\": 39, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu_b_forward\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 14, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T01:29:40.741118Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r8s0 (regression, -13.34%): The zero-masked EX/MEM shift bank preserved adjacent forwarding and CoreMark cycles, with median Gowin Fmax falling from 104.134 to 90.243 MHz as the routed multiply bypass through the two-level ALU B mux and the ALU into the nonshift bank became the critical path.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
