{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short\ngit diff --stat\nsed -n '1,100p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r2s0.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-001-r2s0\ntitle: \"Precompute forwarding matches and flatten EX operand selection\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The 45.918 MHz champion has two nearly tied Gowin setup paths. In the median placements the redirect path reaches 27.072 ns and the multiplier-to-data-memory path reaches 27.067 ns. Both cross the EX operand selection logic. That logic currently combines the register file's write-through mux, EX forwarding and, for ALU operands, a separate PC or immediate mux. Shortening their shared operand path can raise Fmax at the same instruction cadence.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compare both incoming ID source addresses with the current EX and MEM destinations and latch those address matches in ID/EX. Capture one shared copy of the current WB write data and each source's same-edge WB hit alongside the raw register-file values. At EX, qualify the registered matches with the corresponding advanced producer's actual EX/MEM and MEM/WB reg_write controls. This late qualification preserves suppression of trapped writes. Form mutually exclusive selects in priority order EX/MEM, MEM/WB, captured WB, then raw register data. A source of x0 selects zero. Use these selects in parallel AND-OR muxes for the forwarded operands, and fold the AUIPC PC and immediate alternatives into the ALU operand muxes. Branch, store, divider and RVFI sources use the register-only selection.\n\n  Capture and hold the comparison bits and the WB snapshot with the same ID/EX controls as the instruction. While an older dmem request stalls, the held instruction still needs the retained MEM/WB forwarding payload after its retirement-valid bit clears. Use the retained reg_write qualifier for that source and use the writeback unit's actual write enable when recording the same-edge WB hit. Preserve the load-use bubble, redirect and divider hold priorities. The divider continues to use its issue-time source values when it completes.\n\n  An isolated prototype reached 50.225 MHz median across the three Gowin placements. The option-0 worst path fell from 28.171 ns and 15 cells to 25.126 ns and 13 cells. At 4,491,485 marker-bracketed cycles, 50.225 MHz projects to 111.82 CoreMark iterations/s, about +9.4%. Confirm the cycle count and CRCs under both standard bus stalls and rerun the existing formal and co-simulation gates on the implementation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 9\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/reg_file.sv\n    description: \"Add a raw read mode for the integrated core. Keep the existing standalone write-first mode and register reset behavior.\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \"Carry the registered EX and MEM address matches, nonzero source flags, same-edge WB hits and shared WB write data in the ID/EX payload.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Compute both source tags against current EX, MEM and WB destinations. Latch the flags, raw reads and WB snapshot alongside the decoded instruction, with the same hold and flush controls.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered matches and actual downstream reg_write controls to derive mutually exclusive forwarding enables with younger-writer priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Select forwarded operands in parallel from EX/MEM, MEM/WB, sampled WB and raw RF data. Fold PC and immediate selection into the corresponding ALU operand mux.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect raw RF reads, producer destinations and the WB write port to ID, then route the latched matches and the existing forwarding data buses to EX.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise all forwarding priorities, including the same-edge WB snapshot, x0 and a held consumer that must still receive a previously retired WB value during a dmem stall. Check exact channel-0 source values and contiguous order.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
