d the ALU across 156 cells. The four 32-bit division and remainder expressions are the most likely source of that depth. A baseline Verilator RVFI trace with both bus stalls enabled reproduced the logged 4,491,485 marker-to-marker cycles and canonical CRCs. The only two division or remainder retirements were DIVU, one before the start marker and one after the stop marker. This makes divi\n…[28566 of 31638 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:153c8d59aa0627e5]…\nanonical CoreMark passed all CRCs with both stalls enabled and had no out-of-bounds accesses.\\n- CoreMark's start and stop markers landed at cycles 15,185 and 4,206,526. The 4,191,341-cycle window improves iterations per cycle by 7.16% over the stated baseline.\\n\\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| 0 | 5.094 |\\n| 1 | 5.538 |\\n| 2 | 5.538 |\\n| Median | 5.538 |\\n\\nMedian fitness was 13.21 iterations/sec, up 9.0% from the stated 12.12 iterations/sec baseline. Placement option 0 used 12,894 LUT4 and 30 LUT-RAM blocks. The forwarded-operand ALU path remained timing-critical across placements.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T20:04:44.623909Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.99%): The 32-entry partial-tag BTB saved 300,144 stalled CoreMark cycles by avoiding EX squashes on correct predictions, while the forwarded-operand ALU critical path limited median Fmax to 5.538 MHz and left throughput below the round\\u2019s clocked-divider winner.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
