{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    row = json.loads(line)\n    print(row['id'], row['category'], row['fmax_mhz'], row.get('seeds'), row.get('critical_path',{}).get('from'), row.get('critical_path',{}).get('to'))\n    if row['id'] in ['hyp-20261120-001-r2s0','hyp-20261120-002-r1s1']:\n        print(row.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-ec4d1c8 micro_opt 5.442 [5.14, 5.442, 5.442] cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0 dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\nhyp-20261120-001-r1s0 micro_opt 45.881 [42.639, 45.881, 45.881] cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\nhyp-20261120-002-r1s1 structural 45.918 [43.713, 45.918, 45.918] cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0 dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\n# Clocked radix-4 divider\n\n`div_unit.sv` handles DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. It captures forwarded operands,\nunsigned magnitudes and mode at issue. The next edge registers D, 2D and 3D.\nSix recurrence edges process the 36-bit zero-padded dividend in groups of\nthree radix-4 digits. Each digit uses three parallel 35-bit subtractions and\nselects the highest threshold without a borrow. EX/MEM captures the\nsign-corrected quotient or remainder eight cycles after issue when ready.\nDivide-by-zero, signed overflow and the ALTOPS formulas use the same schedule.\n\nEX holds fetch and ID/EX and sends invalid, control-cleared bubbles to EX/MEM\nwhile the divider runs. An unaccepted older memory request holds EX/MEM and\ndelays issue. The divider holds its completed result and original operands\nuntil EX/MEM accepts them. The result uses existing forwarding and channel-0\nretirement. The 36-bit register shifts dividend digits out and quotient digits\nin, sharing storage. A guarded `core_pkg.sv` include in `core.sv` supports the\nrequested alphabetical Verilator lint command.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS configurations.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed 53 of 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks on the\n  first run, including liveness. The periodic `formal-deep` suite was outside\n  this local run.\n- `make test TARGET=bench` passed all six runners. The divider unit tests\n  cover exact RV32M results, 512 seeded arithmetic cases and result retention\n  under backpressure. The pipeline test checks a load-to-divide dependency,\n  dependent consecutive divides, immediate ALU and store consumers, a held\n  older store, and exact channel-0 retirement and store acceptance.\n- Selftest and the three rand\n…[2831 of 5903 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:deb7064d7c1e1b4e]…\noreMark passed the canonical 2K CRC checks with both stalls enabled and reported no out-of-bounds accesses. The markers at cycles 15,801 and 4,507,286 give the champion's 4,491,485-cycle window.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Longest setup path |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 56.544 | Divider recurrence |\n| 1 | 55.338 | EX/MEM write control through the EX ALU to data memory |\n| 2 | 55.338 | EX/MEM write control through the EX ALU to data memory |\n\nThe 55.338 MHz median gives 123.21 CoreMark iterations/s, 20.5% above the champion's 102.23. Option 0 used 3,170 logic cells, 638 registers, 32 LUT-RAM blocks, and four BSRAMs. The median is 0.917 MHz below the prototype's 56.255 MHz, with forwarding control still on the longest path in options 1 and 2.\n\nhyp-20261120-002-r2s1 structural 55.048 [53.862, 55.048, 55.048] cpu/u_ex/u_div/dividend_quotient_q_35_s0 cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_30_s0\nhyp-20261120-003-r2s2 predictor 49.492 [45.808, 49.492, 49.492] cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
