thetic-mount-targets-1002/42eb824eac877172/1572485\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/0cb059a4/codex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1002/42eb824eac877172/1572483\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/0cb059a4/codex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1002/42eb824eac877172/1572484\n/srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/0cb059a4/codex-bwrap-synthetic-mount-targets-1002/00ef4\n…[6129 of 9201 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d6c095f5e4e5255b]…\nlf\n\tpython3 -m tools.eval.fpga . $(TARGET)\n\ntiming:\n\tpython3 -m tools.eval.gowin $(TARGET)\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.c) \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.h) \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.c) \\\n                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.h)\n\t$(MAKE) -f bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/coremark.elf\n\nnext:\n\tAGENT_PROVIDER=$(AGENT) python3 -m tools.orchestrator $(subst --iterations $(N),--iterations 1,$(ORCH_FLAGS)) $(ORCH_TARGET_FLAG)\n\nloop:\nifneq ($(strip $(WORKTREE)),)\n\t@if [ ! -d \"$(WT_PATH)\" ]; then \\\n\t  echo \"[wt] creating branch $(WT_BRANCH) and worktree $(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n\t  if git rev-parse --verify $(WT_BRANCH) >/dev/null 2>&1; then \\\n\t    git worktree add \"$(WT_PATH)\" $(WT_BRANCH); \\\n\t  else \\\n\t    git worktree add -b $(WT_BRANCH) \"$(WT_PATH)\"; \\\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    row = json.loads(line)\n    if row['id']=='hyp-20261120-002-r2s1':\n        print(row.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n    row = json.loads(line)\n    if row['id']=='hyp-20261120-002-r2s1':\n        print(row.get('implementation_notes',''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Bench EX partition\n\n- EX/MEM captures the full forwarded `rs1 + imm` byte address. JALR shares that sum. MEM uses the registered address for dmem, byte lanes, alignment traps, and word-aligned RVFI addresses.\n- EX captures one signed 33-by-33 product and its word select alongside the integer, link, and divide results. Both EX forwarding and MEM/WB receive the result selected after capture. The ALTOPS build captures the original per-op stand-in on the same edge. The divider keeps its existing issue and result schedule.\n- Decode receives raw imem data. Fetch readiness, redirects, and load-use bubbles control ID/EX validity. A redirect fires when its valid EX entry advances and takes priority over a fetch stall. Alignment uses immediate bit 1 for B/J targets and the low-bit carry for JALR. Trapping control transfers report PC+4 and suppress link writes.\n- The multiply registers live in EX, and the EX/MEM bundle exposes the selected result. The unused branch-target and branch-taken fields were removed. MEM/WB qualifies the forwarding write enable on capture and retains it with the producer data during a data stall. Retirement validity clears independently, so a held EX consumer can still use the value after the producer retires.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed for the real datapath and ALTOPS. All six cocotb runners passed. The pipeline tests retain the original multiply vectors and add 512 deterministic operand pairs per variant, checks on adjacent consumers, stalled stores, accepted memory accesses, and JALR redirects and alignment traps.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench JOBS=8 bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks on the first attempt. Real multiplier coverage for this iteration comes from cocotb and ISS comparison.\n- `make bench TARGET=bench` and `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed. Selftest and the three standard random programs matched the ISS in both bus modes, and stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRC gate. The direct Makefile build needs `NRET=1` because its cosim build script defaults to two channels. The orchestrator derives the setting from `core.yaml`.\n- A separate ISS comparison passed 28,290 retirements per bus mode with 512 operand pairs per multiply variant, signed extremes, and dependent load and store sequences.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` and `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` passed. Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 53.862, 55.048, and 55.048 MHz. The median yielded 122.56 iterations/s at 4,491,485 marker cycles, about 19.9% above the 102.23 iterations/s champion. Option 0 used 2,998 logic cells and two DSP blocks. The divider recurrence was its worst setup path.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
