 Gowin option-0 report, the register-file BSRAM launches both the 28.171 ns path through the EX multiplier to data memory and the 28.135 ns branch path back to fetch. Giving the multiplier its own registered stages left the branch path limiting the median to 45.700 MHz. Both paths need faster register operand delivery.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The champion runs at 45.918 MHz median. In the reproduced Gowin option-0 report, the register-file BSRAM launches both the 28.171 ns path through the EX multiplier to data memory and the 28.135 ns branch path back to fetch. Giving the multiplier its own registered sta\n…[35486 of 38558 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1b1974f935264d08]…\nion on a store. The JALR scenario passed 16 stall seeds covering changed, misaligned, and sequential targets, including an older stalled store and an imem stall on the recovery edge.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed. Selftest and all three random programs matched the reference ISS in zero-wait mode and with both bus stalls enabled.\n- The canonical 2K, 10-iteration CoreMark build used `-O3`. With both stalls enabled, it completed in **4,186,330 marker-window cycles** with all five canonical CRCs, the validation literal, and no out-of-bounds accesses.\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 54.258 MHz |\n| 1 | 55.699 MHz |\n| 2 | 55.699 MHz |\n| Median | **55.699 MHz** |\n\n`make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reported **133.05 CoreMark iter/s**, up **7.99%** from the supplied 123.21 iter/s baseline. The worst path in each placement runs through the divider recurrence. Placement option 0 used 3,945 logic cells in the evaluator's area metric, compared with 3,170 on the parent, and 712 registers.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
