{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_12", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n e=json.loads(l)\n if e['id']=='hyp-20261120-001-r3s0':\n  print(json.dumps(e['hypothesis'], indent=2)); print(e['implementation_notes'])\nPY\nls /opt/hwe-toolchain && rg -n 'CROSS|GCC|OBJCOPY' bench/programs/Makefile && sed -n '1,245p' tools/eval/gowin.py\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"motivation\": \"The fetch address is currently the PC register output. An EX redirect\\nsquashes decode even when imem is ready because the target address appears\\nonly after the update edge. A trace of the champion's 4,491,485-cycle\\nCoreMark window counted 294,425 taken conditional branches, 49,367 JALs\\nand 13,735 JALRs. IF/ID is already combinational, so a mux can put the\\nresolved target on the fetch port during the same cycle and reclaim the\\notherwise empty decode slot.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"In IF, select the resolved EX target as the actual fetch address on a\\nredirect and the sequential PC otherwise. Drive both io_imemAddr and the\\ninstruction's decode PC from that selected address. Let ID capture the\\nreturned target instruction at the edge that advances the branch or jump\\nout of EX, provided imem is ready and the pipeline can advance. Store the\\nselected address plus four in the PC on an accepted fetch. If a redirect\\noccurs while fetch cannot advance, store the unincremented target so it\\ncan be retried. Use the actual EX condition and alignment-qualified target.\\nThe fetch address mux is independent of the bus ready inputs.\\n\\nWith the fetch port already selecting the target, remove redirect as a\\nreason to mask the fetched instruction or flush ID/EX. Preserve the bubble\\non imem backpressure and the load-use interlock. With an older dmem request\\nstalled, hold ID/EX and EX/MEM and keep requesting the resolved target.\\nCapture the target entry only when the older request can advance. This\\nallows the target instruction to use ordinary EX/MEM forwarding for an\\nimmediately consumed JAL or JALR link value. Misaligned control transfers\\ncontinue to take the existing trap path and suppress the redirect.\\n\\nA scratch implementation with the selected-address increment reduced the\\nstalled, CRC-validated CoreMark window to 4,136,096 cycles, a 7.91%\\nreduction. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 55.788, 55.797 and\\n55.797 MHz. The median yields 134.90 iterations/s, a 9.49% gain over the\\nchampion. \n…[11033 of 14105 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6790ab95424b202f]…\n:\n            print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: FAILED ({r.get('reason')})\")\n            continue\n        print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: Fmax {r['fmax_mhz']} MHz, {r['levels']} logic levels; \"\n              f\"logic {r['logic']}, registers {r['regs']}, LUT-RAM {r['lutram']}, BSRAM {r['bsram']}, DSP {r['dsp']}\")\n        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n        for i, p in enumerate(critical_paths(tr.read_text(errors=\"replace\"), a.paths), 1):\n            print(f\"  path {i}: {p['arrival_ns']} ns, {p['logic_cells']} cells, {p['from']} -> {p['to']}\")\n            print(f\"          through: {' > '.join(p['modules'])}\")\n        print(f\"  full report: {tr}\")\n    if len(res) > 1 and all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\n        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
