hanges\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_2", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261120-002-r1s1|pipeline.*multipl|multipl.*pipeline|DSP' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a shared iterative divider\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The bench retest reached 5.442 MHz. Its 199.837 ns worst path traverses forwarding, EX, and the ALU across 156 cells. The four 32-bit division and remainder expressions are the most likely source of that depth. A baseline Verilator RVFI trace with both bus stalls enabled reproduced the logged 4,491,485 marker-to-marker cycles and canonical CRCs. The only two division or remainder retirements were DIVU, one before the start marker and one after the stop marker. This makes division latency a low-cost place to trade cycles for clock frequency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench retest reached 5.442 MHz. Its 199.837 ns worst path traverses forwarding, EX, and the ALU across 156 cells. The four 32-bit division and remainder expressions are the most likely source of that depth. A baseline Verilator RVFI trace with both bus stalls enabled reproduced the logged 4,491,485 marker-to-marker cycles and canonical CRCs. The only two division or remainder retirements were DIVU, one before the start marker and one after the stop marker. This makes division latency a low-cost place to trade cycles for clock frequency.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Use one restoring divider for all four operations. On a valid EX issue, capture the forwarded operands, their magnitudes, and the quotient/remainder and sign controls. Process five dividend bits per cycle for seven iterations, with three leading zero bits before the 32-bit magnitude. At each step, shift the next dividend bit into a 33-bit trial remainder, subtract the divisor, and use the borrow to select the next remainder and quotient bit. Apply sign correction from the registered final state during result transfer, outside the recurrence. A signed quotient truncates toward zero, and a signed remainder follows the dividend sign. Handle zero divisors explicitly with an all-ones quotient or the original dividend as remainder. Return INT_MI\n…[18475 of 21547 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:04b031626815f712]…\n-0 retirement and store acceptance.\\n- Selftest and the three random trace ELFs matched the Python ISS with\\n  zero-wait buses and with both stalls enabled. Stalled CoreMark passed UART\\n  and CRC validation.\\n\\n## Gowin and CoreMark\\n\\n| Metric | Baseline | Clocked divider |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Option-0 worst setup path (ns) | 199.837 | 28.171 |\\n| Option-0 worst path logic cells | 156 | 15 |\\n| Median Fmax (MHz) | 5.442 | 45.918 |\\n| CoreMark marker cycles | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\\n| Fitness (iterations/s) | 12.12 | 102.23 |\\n| Gowin logic cells | 12,312 | 3,089 |\\n| Flip-flops | 460 | 664 |\\n\\nThe placement options measured 43.713, 45.918 and 45.918 MHz. The option-0\\nworst path now runs from the register file through ID and the EX ALU to data\\nmemory. Fitness rose 743.48%, above the 4.6% threshold. The added latency\\napplies to divide and remainder instructions, which were absent inside the\\nbaseline CoreMark timing markers.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T19:55:46.525944Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 1}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
