{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg\ncat formal/checks-deep.cfg\nsed -n '1,230p' cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progre\n…[7654 of 10726 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5b252075b0711f18]…\n(1, 33)) or 1\n        q, r = divmod(a, b)\n        await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIVU, a, b, q)\n        await _check_div(dut, ALU_REMU, a, b, r)\n\n        signed_a = a if a < 0x80000000 else a - (1 << 32)\n        signed_b = (b & 0x7FFFFFFF) or 1\n        if rng.getrandbits(1):\n            signed_b = -signed_b\n        q = abs(signed_a) // abs(signed_b)\n        if (signed_a < 0) != (signed_b < 0):\n            q = -q\n        await _check_div(dut, ALU_DIV, signed_a, signed_b, q)\n        await _check_div(dut, ALU_REM, signed_a, signed_b, signed_a - q * signed_b)\n\n\ndef test_alu_runner(monkeypatch):\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"COCOTB_TEST_FILTER\", r\"^test_alu\\.(?!divide_)\")\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"alu\",\n               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"alu.sv\"],\n               test_module=\"test_alu\")\n\n\ndef test_div_unit_runner(monkeypatch):\n    monkeypatch.setenv(\"COCOTB_TEST_FILTER\", r\"^test_alu\\.divide_\")\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"div_unit\",\n               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"div_unit.sv\"],\n               test_module=\"test_alu\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
