{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-001-r3s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]); print(d[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-001-r3s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]); print(d[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"In IF, select the resolved EX target as the actual fetch address on a\nredirect and the sequential PC otherwise. Drive both io_imemAddr and the\ninstruction's decode PC from that selected address. Let ID capture the\nreturned target instruction at the edge that advances the branch or jump\nout of EX, provided imem is ready and the pipeline can advance. Store the\nselected address plus four in the PC on an accepted fetch. If a redirect\noccurs while fetch cannot advance, store the unincremented target so it\ncan be retried. Use the actual EX condition and alignment-qualified target.\nThe fetch address mux is independent of the bus ready inputs.\n\nWith the fetch port already selecting the target, remove redirect as a\nreason to mask the fetched instruction or flush ID/EX. Preserve the bubble\non imem backpressure and the load-use interlock. With an older dmem request\nstalled, hold ID/EX and EX/MEM and keep requesting the resolved target.\nCapture the target entry only when the older request can advance. This\nallows the target instruction to use ordinary EX/MEM forwarding for an\nimmediately consumed JAL or JALR link value. Misaligned control transfers\ncontinue to take the existing trap path and suppress the redirect.\n\nA scratch implementation with the selected-address increment reduced the\nstalled, CRC-validated CoreMark window to 4,136,096 cycles, a 7.91%\nreduction. Gowin placement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 55.788, 55.797 and\n55.797 MHz. The median yields 134.90 iterations/s, a 9.49% gain over the\nchampion. At that cycle count, a median above 53.305 MHz clears the\ntournament threshold. The longest paths remained in the EX-to-data-memory\ndatapath, with the divider recurrence close behind.\n\nThe scratch implementation passed all 53 single-retire ALTOPS formal\nchecks, all six cocotb runners, and selftest plus three random programs\nagainst the ISS with zero-wait and stalled buses. Directed tests passed for\nadjacent target retirement with link forwarding and for target retry with\nsimultaneous instruction and data backpressure.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'set -e\nbench_scratch=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/bench-redirect.XXXXXX\")\ncp -R Makefile bench fpga test \"$bench_scratch/\"\nmkdir -p \"$bench_scratch/cores/bench\"\ncp -R cores/bench/rtl cores/bench/test cores/bench/core.yaml \"$bench_scratch/cores/bench/\"\nprintf '\"'%s\\\\n' \\\"\"'$bench_scratch\"\npython3 - \"$bench_scratch\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nrtl = Path(sys.argv[1]) / 'cores/bench/rtl'\np = rtl / 'ex_stage.sv'\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('  assign redirect = ex_valid && \"'!stall && control_taken && !target_misaligned;'\"', '  assign redirect = ex_valid && control_taken && \"'!target_misaligned;'\"')\np.write_text(s)\np = rtl / 'hazard_unit.sv'\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('    flush_id      = load_use_hazard || redirect;', '    flush_id      = load_use_hazard;')\ns = s.replace('  input  logic       redirect,          // EX has resolved a branch/jump\\\\n', '')\ns = s.replace('  output logic       stall_id,', '  output logic       advance_redirect,  // older data request can advance\\\\n  output logic       stall_id,')\ns = s.replace('    stall_if      =', '    advance_redirect = \"'!dmem_stall;'\"\\\\n    stall_if      =')\np.write_text(s)\np = rtl / 'core.sv'\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('  logic        redirect;', '  logic        redirect, advance_redirect;')\ns = s.replace('    .redirect_target (redirect_target),\\\\n    .imem_addr', '    .redirect_target (redirect_target),\\\\n    .advance_redirect(advance_redirect),\\\\n    .imem_addr')\ns = s.replace('    .redirect       (redirect),\\\\n    .divide_wait', '    .advance_redirect(advance_redirect),\\\\n    .divide_wait')\np.write_text(s)\np = rtl / 'if_stage.sv'\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('  output logic [31:0] imem_addr,', '  input  logic        advance_redirect,\\\\n  output logic [31:0] imem_addr,')\ns = s.replace('    else if (redirect) pc <= redirect_target;\\\\n    else if (\"'!stall)   pc <= pc + 32'\"\\\\'d4;', '    else if (\"'!stall)   pc <= imem_addr + 32'\"\\\\'d4;\\\\n    else if (redirect && advance_redirect) pc <= redirect_target;')\ns = s.replace('  assign imem_addr = pc;', '  assign imem_addr = redirect ? redirect_target : pc;')\ns = s.replace('    out.pc    = pc;', '    out.pc    = imem_addr;')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
