ch it in EX/MEM. Drive data memory, byte lanes, alignment checks, and the corresponding RVFI address from that register. The general result mux and all M-extension outputs stay off the data-memory address cone.\\n\\nForm one signed 33-by-33 product from the forwarded operands, sign-extending rs1 only for MULH and MULHSU and rs2 only for MULH. Capture the low 64 bits and a word-select tag alongside the integer result on the existing EX/MEM edge. Select the appropriate registered word for forwarding and writeback, with the same immediate-consumer latency as the champion. Keep the exact ALTOPS mult\n…[22482 of 25554 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ccc18c43099f90e5]…\ncovery address to imem and decode, and retry that address if imem is stalled. Select the predicted successor on acceptance.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register the lookup state and prediction bit with each instruction and retain them on a hold.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register the prediction mismatch and its resolved successor, export training, and gate wrong-path EX advancement and divider issue.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire registered recovery to fetch and the younger EX kill. Suppress load-use from the killed instruction and allow the corrected fetch into ID.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Add the BTB to the runner and cover taken loops, region aliases, cross-region transfers, and JALR recovery across bus stalls.'}, {'file': 'test/test_branch_predictor.py', 'description': 'Verify that recent writes update a stale lookup snapshot and that a newer conflicting tag takes precedence over an older hit.'}]}\nimplementation_notes=\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
