{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'git status --short --untracked-files=all && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-003-r1s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-003-r1s2\ntitle: \"Predict branch and jump targets with a compact fetch BTB\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Fetch always advances to PC+4 today. An aligned taken branch or jump\n  resolved in EX squashes the one younger fetch opportunity, even for a\n  loop back edge or return that repeatedly takes the same target. A fetch-PC\n  lookup can remove these bubbles without putting instruction memory or an\n  instruction-derived target adder on the fetch next-PC path. The logged\n  worst path is in the forwarded-operand ALU path. A cycle replay of the\n  canonical CoreMark retirement trace reproduced the 4,491,485 baseline\n  marker-window cycles under both bus stalls. The 32-entry table reduced\n  the modeled count to 4,191,341 cycles (+7.16% iterations per cycle).\n  Doubling the table recovered only another 5,011 cycles, so the smaller\n  table limits fetch mux depth and FPGA area.\nhypothesis: |\n  Add a 32-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer with a two-bit saturating\n  direction counter. Index by PC[6:2] and tag by PC[19:7]. Predict the cached\n  target on a valid tag hit with the counter MSB set. Use PC+4 on other fetches.\n  Admit only word-aligned sources and targets in the 1 MiB instruction\n  window. Store target[19:2] and reconstruct the aligned address with zero\n  upper bits. Clear the valid bits at reset and leave payload RAM unreset\n  so the FPGA can infer distributed memory. This window limits prediction\n  coverage while the architecturally computed successor retains all 32 bits.\n\n  Train only when a valid, trap-free EX control-flow instruction advances.\n  Allocate a taken control transfer on a miss. For a conditional branch,\n  initialize weakly taken on allocation, increment on taken hits, and\n  decrement on not-taken hits. Refresh the target on every taken update.\n  Set a resolved JAL or JALR to strongly taken with its latest target.\n  Ignore an out-of-window target for training. Keep targets in a separate\n  fetch-only RAM so EX training needs to read only the tag and counter.\n\n  When ID accepts an instruction, advance the fetch PC to its prediction.\n  Use the current fetch PC as that instruction's predicted successor in EX.\n  The two positions hold together on a dmem stall, and an imem stall or\n  load-use bubble admits no new EX instruction. Compare the full fetch PC\n  with the valid EX instruction's architectural next PC, including PC+4 for\n  non-controls and suppressed misaligned transfers. Recover on mismatch,\n  kill the younger fetch, and give recovery priority over imem backpressure\n  once EX can advance. This covers stale hits on non-controls, wrong targets\n  and both direction errors. RVFI continues to report the resolved next PC.\n\n  At the replayed cycle count, the acceptance threshold permits about a\n  2.4% drop in median Gowin Fmax. Verify marker-window cycles and median\n  Fmax with the existing eval flow. Exercise a warm taken loop, loop exit,\n  changed JALR target, and recovery coincident with bus stalls using the\n  existing retirement checks.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/branch_predictor.sv\n    description: \"Implement the tagged target and direction table, including reset validity, independent lookup and training, and bounded aligned target storage.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Advance the PC to the predicted successor when ID accepts the fetch and give EX recovery priority over instruction stalls.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the full architectural successor and valid resolved control outcome for recovery and predictor training. Preserve link and trap semantics.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the predictor and compare the fetch PC with the EX successor. Qualify recovery and training by EX advancement and drive the existing pipeline flush on mismatch.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
