{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    record = json.loads(line)\n    if record['id'] == 'hyp-20261120-002-r1s1':\n        print(record['implementation_notes'])\nPY\nrg -n 'GOWIN|gowin.*sh|perturb|timing' tools/eval/gowin.py | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n    record = json.loads(line)\n    if record['id'] == 'hyp-20261120-002-r1s1':\n        print(record['implementation_notes'])\nPY\nrg -n 'GOWIN|gowin.*sh|perturb|timing' tools/eval/gowin.py | head -50\"", "aggregated_output": "# Clocked radix-4 divider\n\n`div_unit.sv` handles DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU. It captures forwarded operands,\nunsigned magnitudes and mode at issue. The next edge registers D, 2D and 3D.\nSix recurrence edges process the 36-bit zero-padded dividend in groups of\nthree radix-4 digits. Each digit uses three parallel 35-bit subtractions and\nselects the highest threshold without a borrow. EX/MEM captures the\nsign-corrected quotient or remainder eight cycles after issue when ready.\nDivide-by-zero, signed overflow and the ALTOPS formulas use the same schedule.\n\nEX holds fetch and ID/EX and sends invalid, control-cleared bubbles to EX/MEM\nwhile the divider runs. An unaccepted older memory request holds EX/MEM and\ndelays issue. The divider holds its completed result and original operands\nuntil EX/MEM accepts them. The result uses existing forwarding and channel-0\nretirement. The 36-bit register shifts dividend digits out and quotient digits\nin, sharing storage. A guarded `core_pkg.sv` include in `core.sv` supports the\nrequested alphabetical Verilator lint command.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS configurations.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed 53 of 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks on the\n  first run, including liveness. The periodic `formal-deep` suite was outside\n  this local run.\n- `make test TARGET=bench` passed all six runners. The divider unit tests\n  cover exact RV32M results, 512 seeded arithmetic cases and result retention\n  under backpressure. The pipeline test checks a load-to-divide dependency,\n  dependent consecutive divides, immediate ALU and store consumers, a held\n  older store, and exact channel-0 retirement and store acceptance.\n- Selftest and the three random trace ELFs matched the Python ISS with\n  zero-wait buses and with both stalls enabled. Stalled CoreMark passed UART\n  and CRC validation.\n\n## Gowin and CoreMark\n\n| Metric | Baseline | Clocked divider |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Option-0 worst setup path (ns) | 199.837 | 28.171 |\n| Option-0 worst path logic cells | 156 | 15 |\n| Median Fmax (MHz) | 5.442 | 45.918 |\n| CoreMark marker cycles | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\n| Fitness (iterations/s) | 12.12 | 102.23 |\n| Gowin logic cells | 12,312 | 3,089 |\n| Flip-flops | 460 | 664 |\n\nThe placement options measured 43.713, 45.918 and 45.918 MHz. The option-0\nworst path now runs from the register file through ID and the EX ALU to data\nmemory. Fitness rose 743.48%, above the 4.6% threshold. The added latency\napplies to divide and remainder instructions, which were absent inside the\nbaseline CoreMark timing markers.\n\n1:\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n4:route and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\n22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\n23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\n35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n61:        \"set_option -gen_text_timing_rpt 1\",\n77:    modules the path crosses (in order), from Gowin's timing report.\"\"\"\n114:        return {\"placement_failed\": True, \"fmax_mhz\": None, \"reason\": \"no Fmax in timing report\"}\n133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n155:    # Plain threads and blocking waits, no asyncio: agents run `make timing`\n192:        \"perturbations\": [[r[\"place_option\"], r[\"fmax_mhz\"], r[\"levels\"]] for r in results],\n200:    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\n214:                                wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\", options=opts)\n221:        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
