{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && ls -la cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +742.82%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM with a shared five-bit-per-cycle restoring divider shortened the EX critical path and raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 45.881 MHz, while CoreMark stayed at 4,491,485 measured cycles under bus stalls with both DIVU instructions paying their extra latency outside the timed region.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.99%): The 32-entry partial-tag BTB saved 300,144 stalled CoreMark cycles by avoiding EX squashes on correct predictions, while the forwarded-operand ALU critical path limited median Fmax to 5.538 MHz and left throughput below the round’s clocked-divider winner.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (improvement, +20.52%): Asynchronous LUT RAM reads removed BSRAM clock-to-output delay from the multiply and branch operand paths, and registering forwarding tag matches at ID/EX let EX use one-hot operand selection, raising median Fmax from 45.918 to 55.338 MHz at the same stalled CoreMark cycle count.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 (regression, +19.89%): Separately registering the effective address and multiply product at EX/MEM and using valid bits to squash younger instructions removed the multiplier from the BRAM address path and instruction masking from fetch-PC feedback, raising median Fmax to 55.048 MHz at the same stalled CoreMark cycle count and exposing the divider recurrence as the worst setup path in placement option 0.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (regression, +15.50%): With EX-to-BTB training registered on the clocked-divider core, the ALU path limited median Fmax to 49.492 MHz, below the 51.64 MHz the 32-entry BTB needed for its 300,144-cycle savings on stalled CoreMark to beat the round’s register-file and forwarding optimization.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +9.49%): With combinational IF/ID, feeding the resolved EX target to imem and the decode PC removed the redirect bubble on accepted fetches and cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 7.91%, with the remaining EX-to-\n…[1325 of 4397 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bccd20ecb8c67cbe]…\nmemory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\ntotal 16\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 22:07 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 20 22:07 ..\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
