{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'predictor|btb|redirect cycle' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json;[(print(n, json.dumps(j,indent=2))) for n,l in (x.split(\\\":\\\",1) for x in sys.stdin) for j in [json.loads(l)]]'\"", "aggregated_output": "4 {\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261120-003-r1s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Predict branches and jumps with a 32-entry partial-tag BTB\",\n  \"category\": \"predictor\",\n  \"motivation\": \"Fetch always advances to PC+4 today. An aligned taken branch or jump\\nresolved in EX squashes the one younger fetch opportunity, even for a\\nloop back edge or return that repeatedly takes the same target. A fetch-PC\\nlookup supplies a cached target in parallel with instruction memory so a\\ncorrect prediction removes the squash cycle. A 32-entry scratch RTL\\nprototype with seven-bit tags cut canonical CoreMark marker-window\\ncycles from 4,491,485 to 4,191,341 under both bus stalls (+7.16%\\niterations per cycle). Gowin placement options measured 5.077, 5.482,\\nand 5.482 MHz, for 5.482 MHz median and 13.08 iter/sec (+7.9% versus\\n12.12). Gowin reported 12,766 LUT4 and 30 LUT-RAM blocks for placement\\noption 0 and identified the forwarded-operand ALU path as critical.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"Fetch always advances to PC+4 today. An aligned taken branch or jump\\nresolved in EX squashes the one younger fetch opportunity, even for a\\nloop back edge or return that repeatedly takes the same target. A fetch-PC\\nlookup supplies a cached target in parallel with instruction memory so a\\ncorrect prediction removes the squash cycle. A 32-entry scratch RTL\\nprototype with seven-bit tags cut canonical CoreMark marker-window\\ncycles from 4,491,485 to 4,191,341 under both bus stalls (+7.16%\\niterations per cycle). Gowin placement options measured 5.077, 5.482,\\nand 5.482 MHz, for 5.482 MHz median and 13.08 iter/sec (+7.9% versus\\n12.12). Gowin reported 12,766 LUT4 and 30 LUT-RAM blocks for placement\\noption 0 and identified the forwarded-operand ALU path as critical.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 32-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer with a two-bit saturating\\ndirection counter. Index by PC[6:2] and use PC[13:7] as the partial tag.\\nPredict the cached target on a valid tag hit with the counter MSB set.\\nUse PC+4 on other fetches. Qualify fetch hits and trainin\n…[37153 of 40225 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1634db0ad7925435]…\nvalidation literal, and no out-of-bounds accesses.\\n\\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| 0 | 54.258 MHz |\\n| 1 | 55.699 MHz |\\n| 2 | 55.699 MHz |\\n| Median | **55.699 MHz** |\\n\\n`make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reported **133.05 CoreMark iter/s**, up **7.99%** from the supplied 123.21 iter/s baseline. The worst path in each placement runs through the divider recurrence. Placement option 0 used 3,945 logic cells in the evaluator's area metric, compared with 3,170 on the parent, and 712 registers.\\n\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T21:04:52.981602Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 3,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r3s2 (regression, +7.99%): Registering the selected writeback data in MEM/WB and moving AUIPC to the PC-relative adder shifted the 64-entry BTB core\\u2019s critical path from WB forwarding through the ALU to the divider, and at the resulting 55.699 MHz median, saving 305,155 stalled CoreMark cycles yielded 133.05 iter/s against the shorter-divider variant\\u2019s 138.68 iter/s.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
