{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'gw_sh|GOWIN' tools/eval/gowin.py setup.sh\nrg 'hyp-20261121-001-r(7|8|10)s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n x=json.loads(l); print(x[\\\"id\\\"]); print(x.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\"))\n'\"", "aggregated_output": "tools/eval/gowin.py:22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\ntools/eval/gowin.py:128:def _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\nhyp-20261121-001-r7s0\nForm the default operands before the ID/EX edge. For each register\nsource, capture the register-file word when neither eligible bypass\nproducer matches and capture zero otherwise. In a separate ALU-B\nword, capture the immediate for immediate operations or the same\ndefault register word for register operations. Retain the raw\nimmediate for addresses and PC displacements and the independently\ncaptured rs2 for branch, store, multiply, divide, and RVFI operands.\nFor immediate ALU-B operations, disable every ALU-B bypass term in ID.\nGroup the six remaining EX bypass terms into three explicit pairs\nper bit, pairing ADD with SUB, other with MEM/WB, and multiply-low\nwith multiply-high. Each pair needs just four LUT inputs to compute\ntwo masked bits and their OR. OR the three pair outputs with the\ncaptured default, giving four inputs to the final reduction.\nApply the same structure to rs1, rs2, and ALU B.\n\nRetain EX priority over MEM, x0 behavior, fallback to older values\nafter a trapping producer, the load-use bubble, and lockstep holding\nof operand defaults and bypass enables under data backpressure. The\nEX/MEM lanes and MEM/WB capture keep their current timing.\n\nThe scratch implementation passed canonical CoreMark in 4,148,503\nmarker cycles and matched the ISS on selftest and the three random\nprograms with zero-wait and stalled buses. Gowin reported 91.249,\n103.152, and 103.152 MHz. The 103.152 MHz median yields 248.65 iter/s,\na 7.46% gain. Placement option 0 us\n…[2647 of 5719 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e2c3bad923db50b2]…\nll queue declines normal imem responses.\n\nA scratch implementation with raw divider wait feeding both ID stall and\nnormal IF issue passed the pipeline suite and reproduced all canonical\nCRCs in 3,750,582 marker cycles. Placements measured 99.930, 104.930,\nand 104.930 MHz, or 279.77 iter/s. The median placements then had nearly\ntied paths from exact replay validation to queue occupancy and from\nforwarded EX results to branch repair. The pilot gains 3.3%, below the\nrequired 4.6%. To shorten the remaining dequeue path, register whether\na newly accepted guessed slot will be the head. For a normal enqueue,\nthis is true if the queue was empty or if it had one slot and popped.\nQualify the saved bit with the existing registered guess. This removes\nthe checked-slot versus head-pointer comparison from the cycle that\ncombines exact validation with dequeue. Retain the checked-slot index\nfor writing replay metadata. The extra change is unmeasured. The target\nis about 106.6 MHz, above the 106.214 MHz acceptance boundary.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
