{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_49", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261121-001-r10s0|hyp-20261121-001-r11s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r10s0 Compute normal enqueue and dequeue credits independently of EX repair.\nEnqueue on imem ready with free space unless exact replay validation\nrejects the response. Dequeue when dmem, divide, and load-use hazards\nallow issue and the nonempty head consumes its last lane. Update the\none-hot count from those two credits. Reset selects zero slots. Repair\nuses imem ready directly to select either the corrected bus word in\nslot zero or an empty queue that retries the corrected PC. Apply the\nsame priority to the head, tail, lane and\nissue-word selection. A younger divide may assert its raw wait predicate\nin the repair cycle. Clear ID/EX valid on that edge regardless of the\nwait, inhibit divider launch and result acceptance, and retain the\nresolver in EX/MEM and its existing MEM/WB hold. Preserve the exact replay\ncheck and the rule that a full queue declines normal imem responses.\n\nA scratch implementation with raw divider wait feeding both ID stall and\nnormal IF issue passed the pipeline suite and reproduced all canonical\nCRCs in 3,750,582 marker cycles. Placements measured 99.930, 104.930,\nand 104.930 MHz, or 279.77 iter/s. The median placements then had nearly\ntied paths from exact replay validation to queue occupancy and from\nforwarded EX results to branch repair. The pilot gains 3.3%, below the\nrequired 4.6%. To shorten the remaining dequeue path, register whether\na newly accepted guessed slot will be the head. For a normal enqueue,\nthis is true if the queue was empty or if it had one slot and popped.\nQualify the saved bit with the existing registered guess. This removes\nthe checked-slot versus head-pointer comparison from the cycle that\ncombines exact validation with dequeue. Retain the checked-slot index\nfor writing replay metadata. The extra change is unmeasured. The target\nis about 106.6 MHz, above the 106.214 MHz acceptance boundary.\n\nhyp-20261121-001-r11s0 Compute the EX producer match from registered ID/EX validity, validated\ndestination write control, and the current jump alignment result\n…[1043 of 4115 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:844fbc9b0c4eda03]…\n over a raw younger divide wait. Reset the replay lane to\nthe corrected bus word so only the corrected queue can use a replay PC.\n\nA scratch implementation of the two EX qualifiers passed trace cosim\nand canonical stalled CoreMark with the same 3,750,582 marker cycles.\nGowin placements measured 96.990, 103.983 and 103.983 MHz, or\n277.24 iterations/s at the median. EX result forwarding into the shared\ninteger result lane limited the median placements. A scratch build\nwith the fetch qualification also passed trace cosim and reproduced\nthe marker count. Its Gowin median is pending. Localizing fetch\nqualification could relieve repair fanout enough to place the other\npaths better. At the measured cycle\ncount the acceptance threshold is above 106.215 MHz. A 107 MHz median\nwould yield about 285.3 iterations/s.\nMeasure all placements, and exercise a repaired JALR into a divide,\na wrong-path divide, adjacent divide consumers, held dmem responses,\nand fallback forwarding after a trapping jump with the existing gates.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
