{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261121-001-r8s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; r=json.load(sys.stdin); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]); print(r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"Split the current EX/MEM other-result word into two zero-masked banks. One bank captures SLL, SRL, and SRA using registered ID/EX shift enables. The second bank captures the remaining integer and special results. Use one shared other-result tag for both banks. On every advancing edge, a bank supplies zero when its operation class is inactive. A shift still forwards to the immediately following instruction.\n\nPreserve two LUT4 levels per forwarded operand. Combine the two registered banks and their shared tag in one LUT3. Combine the masked MEM/WB word and the prequalified ID/EX default in another LUT3. The ADD/SUB pair and multiply-low/high pair each occupy one LUT4. Reduce those four terms in a final LUT4. MEM merges the two banks under the same tag for writeback.\n\nPreserve direct target fetch, exact RVFI source values, the existing load-use interlock, and stall-aligned forwarding. Exercise adjacent shift consumers, all shift amounts and signedness, and dmem holds across bank changes. A preliminary prototype that also changed branch and compare logic reached 97.008 MHz. Isolate the bank split on the champion's current comparator and one-hot forwarding controls. With the same cycle count, acceptance requires a median above approximately 108.93 MHz. A 110 MHz median would yield about 265.16 iter/s. The timing target is unverified and the divide and branch paths may cap the median after the split. Run the unmodified formal and cosim gates and measure all three Gowin placements.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
