{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && ls -a && ls -a cores/bench/experiments && ls -a cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses | tail -18 && cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n.\n..\n.agents\n.aws\n.codex\n.git\n.gitignore\nARCHITECTURE.md\nCLAUDE.md\nLICENSE\nMakefile\nNOTICE\nbench\ncores\nformal\nfpga\nschemas\nsetup.sh\ntest\ntools\n.\n..\n.gitkeep\nhypotheses\nlog.jsonl\nprogress.png\n.\n..\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (regression, +742.82%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM with a shared five-bit-per-cycle restoring divider shortened the EX critical path and raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 45.881 MHz, while CoreMark stayed at 4,491,485 measured cycles under bus stalls with both DIVU instructions paying their extra latency outside the timed region.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.99%): The 32-entry partial-tag BTB saved 300,144 stalled CoreMark cycles by avoiding \n…[9823 of 12895 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6d08e34a48af7010]…\n, below the 102.55 MHz acceptance floor.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r11s2 (regression, -7.61%): Replaying a terminal B/JAL and fetching its predicted successor saved 71,095 stalled CoreMark cycles, with EX operand forwarding into `train_direct` and terminal-counter lookup into `write_predict_terminal_q` limiting median Gowin Fmax to 92.042 MHz and erasing the throughput gain.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r12s0 (regression, +2.49%): With prefix carries for offsets 0–2, LW-to-load forwarding left RAM-to-address feedback outside the top 25 setup paths, with JALR correction into fetch capping median Gowin Fmax at 98.923 MHz, below the 100.962 MHz needed to win after the address and BEQ/BNE bypasses saved 185,459 stalled CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r12s2 (regression, -3.30%): Replaying through not-taken branches in four-word target prefixes saved 56,957 stalled CoreMark cycles, leaving a 104.60 MHz median Fmax requirement for acceptance that the earlier placement trial missed at 96.595 MHz.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
