t\\nforwarding and same-cycle direct target fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Form the default operands before the ID/EX edge. For each register\\nsource, capture the register-file word when neither eligible bypass\\nproducer matches and capture zero otherwise. In a separate ALU-B\\nword, capture the immediate for immediate operations or the same\\ndefault register word for register operations. Retain the raw\\nimmediate for addresses and PC displacements and th\n…[27341 of 30413 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3fa5671124a3649c]…\n paths. Use the\\nexisting cosim and formal gates and check load pairs with held data\\nresponses, misalignment, and taken and untaken repairs.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry pair type, source matches, and small offset controls in the existing pipeline payloads.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/id_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Qualify immediate load dependencies eligible for direct response forwarding and capture their ordinary operand fallbacks.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Exempt eligible pairs from the load-use bubble while keeping held requests, reset, and repair priorities.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/core.sv\", \"description\": \"Route pair eligibility, the ready memory word, exact load result for RVFI, and the partial equality predicates.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Compare raw active load-byte lanes against the expected branch operand and check sign or zero extension in parallel.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
