{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r9s2\\\",\\\"r11s0\\\",\\\"r11s1\\\",\\\"r12s0\\\",\\\"r12s1\\\",\\\"r12s2\\\",\\\"r8s0\\\",\\\"r8s1\\\",\\\"r9s0\\\",\\\"r9s1\\\",\\\"r7s1\\\")):\n  print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"category\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r.get(\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"),r.get(\\\"cycles\\\"),r.get(\\\"dsp\\\"),r.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"),r.get(\\\"seeds\\\"))\n  print(str(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))[-1250:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-002-r7s1 structural Keep low multiply on a narrower execute bypass 97.608 4148503 6 {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_data_29_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/use_redirect_pc_q_s0', 'slack_ns': -5.763, 'arrival_ns': 16.057, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']} [92.912, 97.608, 97.608]\nble.\n- The timing pass uses two 16-bit branch comparisons. It selects the wide divide remainder within groups of four candidates, then among groups, and uses a shared conditional two's-complement expression for sign correction. The divider keeps its existing cycle count.\n- Cocotb retains the existing multiply vectors and checks all four variants with dependent ALU, branch, and store consumers, including older dmem stalls and held MEM/WB forwarding. It also checks exact operands, contiguous retirement order, unused-field aliases, x0 destinations, and immediate and register shifts.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed in the hardware and ALTOPS configurations. All six cocotb runners passed.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks for the final RTL. No formal fixes were needed.\n- Selftest and all three random programs matched the ISS with and without both bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced the canonical CRCs in 4,148,503 marker cycles.\n- Gowin placements measured 92.912, 97.608, and 97.608 MHz with six DSPs. The 97.608 MHz median yields 235.28 CoreMark iterations/s, below the 100.8 MHz timing target. The median placements are limited by forwarding from the low product into branch redirect.\n\nhyp-20261121-001-r8s0 micro_opt Register shifts in a separate execute result bank 90.243 4148503 4 {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_b_default_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.result.other_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.116, 'arrival_ns': 16.41, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu_b_forward', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} [89.963, 90.243, 90.243]\n\nhyp-20261121-002-r8s1 structural Partition the divider by operand magnitude and isolate its result 107.69 4148503 4 {'fro\n…[9192 of 12264 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:634a44e12ef3cab3]…\ns, both cursor banks, exact alias rejection, fourth-lane direction update ordering, the instruction window, and FENCE.I.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed. All six cocotb runners passed, including the 38 pipeline scenarios.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` passed. The stalled CoreMark run completed ten iterations in **3,693,625 marker cycles**, 56,957 fewer than the reproduced champion. It produced all five expected CRCs and the validation banner, with `oob:false`.\n- The single-channel `formal/run_all.sh` run was incomplete within the local time budget. Eight of 53 checks had passed, including `ill`, `unique`, and `liveness`. No counterexample was reported and no formal fix attempts were needed.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 were launched on the final RTL. The timing target remains unverified. An earlier trial with the same marker cycle count completed all three placements at 80.156, 96.595, and 96.595 MHz. Its 96.595 MHz median was below the 104.60 MHz required at this cycle count.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
