{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r8s1\\\",\\\"r11s1\\\",\\\"r12s1\\\",\\\"r6s1\\\",\\\"r9s2\\\")):\n  print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"] if \\\"fmax_mhz\\\" in r else None)\n  if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r8s1\\\",\\\"r12s1\\\")): print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"],r.get(\\\"error\\\"))\n  else:\n   notes=r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\") or \\\"\\\"\n   print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(l for l in notes.splitlines() if \\\"timing\\\" in l.lower() or \\\"limited\\\" in l.lower() or \\\"trial\\\" in l.lower()))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r6s1 95.991\n## Timing changes\nhyp-20261121-002-r8s1 107.69\nCapture the original forwarded operands and signedness at divider\nissue, then convert to magnitudes during setup. Use the remaining\nslots for one of three exact lanes selected by divisor magnitude D:\n\n- D < 4096: use a registered 4096-entry floor(2**32 / D)\n  reciprocal ROM and the existing multiply and correction scheme.\n  Saturate the D=1 entry, handle D=0 explicitly, and retain 13\n  bits of the scaled estimate and remainder for exact correction.\n  Use nested 256-entry ROM generation blocks for Gowin elaboration.\n- 4096 <= D < 131072: seed the remainder with the top 12 dividend\n  bits and process the remaining 20 bits in five radix-16 steps.\n  The remainder is below D, so only 17 state bits and 21 trial\n  bits are needed. Use parallel threshold subtractions and select\n  the largest nonnegative difference.\n- D >= 131072: seed with the top 17 dividend bits and process the\n  remaining 15 bits in five radix-8 steps. Use only seven full-width\n  threshold subtractions with a 35-bit trial.\n\nKeep the existing divider phase count and hold finished results and\noriginal source words until EX can accept them. Give a completed\ndivide the same result class as SUB and capture its word on that\nEX/MEM lane. SUB and divide are mutually exclusive for each\ninstruction. Use their decode-time one-hot enables to combine the\ntwo words at the register input, with the divider term qualified\nby completion. This moves the divide term off the shared integer\nand special result path, keeps the existing EX bypass fan-in, and\nlets adjacent consumers use the ordinary EX/MEM bypass. Keep\nexact ALTOPS substitutes in the same lane and preserve RV32M corner\ncases, request stability and ordered channel-0 retirement.\n\nA scratch prototype of the divider lanes passed the existing\ndivider tests and canonical stalled CoreMark in 4,148,503 marker\ncycles. Its 100.661 MHz median shifted the timing limit to branch\nresolution with the shared EX result lane nearly tied. A separate\nMEM/\n…[6766 of 9838 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a18d93f9296a707b]…\nd\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:36 (96)\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:36 (96)\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: pc_fwd_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_61 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\n\nFull run log: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-002-r12s1/formal/last_run-h5794090eee034aa.log\nPer-check logs in: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-002-r12s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-h5794