{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r11s1\\\",\\\"r12s0\\\")):\n  print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261121-002-r11s1 \nhyp-20261121-001-r12s0 # Adjacent load forwarding\n\nDecode prequalifies BEQ/BNE and loads with offsets 0, 1, or 2 from the registered issue word. The accepted pair requires an `rs1` dependency on a nonzero load destination, and the address path requires an LW producer. The ID/EX payload records the pair, the raw `rs2` match, and the two offset bits. Other raw source matches retain the load-use interlock.\n\nThe branch path checks the active raw response bytes and verifies extension in parallel. The independent operand can use the registered default or MEM/WB forwarding. Equality, ordered branches, and load-fed equality all feed the same two EX/MEM comparison registers. The edge also captures the prediction-qualified repair enables and correction PC pair for direct control transfers. MEM completes the comparison and applies its polarity for repair, training, and retirement. The resolver retains its comparison and next PC through the repair hold.\n\nThe address path adds the short offset with prefix reductions and XOR, then captures the full byte address at the regular EX/MEM edge. Data stalls hold both instructions. Misaligned producers provide no load response, so the consumer uses its ordinary forwarded operands. Misaligned consumers follow the usual trap and bus-mask logic. Extended response values reach RVFI independently of the timed branch and address paths, including when a load immediate aliases the producer's destination in the raw `rs2` field.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint and all 50 directed pipeline cases passed on the retained RTL. The tests check exact retirement order and operands, byte lanes and extension, carry and wraparound, held responses with invalid data, trapped pairs, and dependencies that retain the interlock. The predictor tests cover taken and untaken repairs with held data and suppression of younger effects.\n- Five-ELF cosim passed, including ISS trace comparisons with and without stalls and stalled CoreMark CRC validation. The canonical run retired the benchmark in 3,565,123 marker cycles, saving 185,459 cycles from the champion.\n- Local formal used the full 53-check single-retirement gate through `formal/run_all.sh` in a scratch copy. The run remained incomplete after twelve passes, including liveness, instruction legality, retirement uniqueness, JALR, and BGEU. No counterexample had been reported.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\nThe retained layout measured 95.642, 98.923, and 98.923 MHz for placement options 0, 1, and 2. The 98.923 MHz median projects to 277.47 iterations per second and falls below the 100.962 MHz acceptance threshold at the measured cycle count.\n\nOption 0 was limited by fetch replay at 10.456 ns, with branch-to-repair at 10.434 ns and branch-to-training at 10.447 ns. Options 1 and 2 were limited by JALR correction into fetch at 10.109 ns, with branch-to-training at 10.086 ns. The data RAM feedback into the effective-address register did not appear among the reported top 25 setup paths for any option.\n\nA trial with unconditional repairs folded into the comparison controls and localized predictor word capture measured 92.556, 96.756, and 96.756 MHz. A further trial moved the JALR successor into EX to shorten its fetch path. Its option 0 measured 91.100 MHz and was limited by ordinary EX operand forwarding into the result lane. Its other reports were pending at the end of the local run.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
