{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261121-(001-r12s0|002-r13s1|003-r13s2)\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; [print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"],sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r12s0\nAdd a MEM-to-EX bypass for a narrowly decoded set of adjacent\nload consumers and let them issue without the ordinary load-use bubble.\nQualify the consumer's opcode, funct3, and source match to the older\nload's nonzero destination. Prequalify the opcode, funct3, and short\nimmediate directly from the registered issue word in parallel with\nnormal instruction decode. Carry the accepted pair type and source\nmatches through ID/EX. Preserve the ordinary interlock for all other\ndependencies.\n\nFor legal BEQ/BNE with rs1 supplied by the older load, compare raw\nresponse bytes against the other operand in MEM. Use the accepted\nload's byte lanes, width, and required sign or zero fill to form two\nequality predicates in parallel. The independent source can use its\nregistered default or existing MEM/WB bypass. If both sources match\nthe load destination, they are equal. Use the round-11 shared branch\nresolution layout. Register two partial predicates and the\nprediction-qualified repair enables at the existing EX/MEM edge.\nOrdinary equality branches supply low and high equality groups.\nOrdered branches supply !high_less and !(high_equal && low_less),\nwhose AND is greater than or equal. On that edge, select and register\nthe correction PC from the prediction and branch type. Finish the\npredicates and apply their polarity to repair and training in MEM.\nKeep the resolver's outcome and next PC through the repair hold.\n\nFor a legal load with offset 0, 1, or 2 whose rs1 comes from an older\nLW, use that ready word as the base of the next effective address.\nCompute the small increment with prefix reductions and XOR so the\ndata RAM path avoids a full variable-operand adder. Capture the full\n32-bit result at the ordinary EX/MEM address edge, and use the normal\nalignment, width, and bus checks in the next MEM cycle. Keep the\npair held while an older request stalls. If the producer traps and\nsupplies no data, use the original forwarded operands. Preserve raw\nRVFI operand values even when an unused instruction field alias\n…[7100 of 10172 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:66cfa1eb327a27a3]…\no terminal counter.\n\nPreserve ordinary decode, execution and EX repair for every replayed\nbranch and JAL. Form the architectural sequential PC by widening\nbefore incrementing the stored word PC. Repair discards younger\ntraces and preserves the resolver and its link. FENCE.I clears\ndescriptor validity, in-flight training and queued replay. Retain\nthe current trap, bus window and single-channel retirement contracts.\n\nA trace-driven model using the evaluator's stall sequence reproduced\nthe champion's marker count and estimates 3,647,865 cycles for this\norganization, 102,717 fewer than the champion. The model assumes\nuninterrupted one-word-per-cycle replay when ID is ready, including\ntrace entry and wrap. At that cycle count the acceptance floor of\n283.19 iterations/s requires a median above 103.31 MHz. A 105 MHz\nmedian would reach 287.84 iterations/s, up 6.3%. Measure replay\nbubbles, source and interior repairs, canonical stalled CoreMark,\nand all three Gowin placements, and run the existing correctness gates.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
