etry the target on the next cycle. Keep the existing load-use interlock, link forwarding, JALR bit-zero clearing, and taken misalignment trap with link-write suppression.\\n\\nReplace the separate fetch and ID/EX PC registers with a shared 30-bit word address and a one-bit increment flag in IF. On every admitted fetch, latch its exact bus word address and set the flag on the edge that captures its instruction in ID/EX. On an advancing redirect with imemReady low, latch the target word address and clear the flag while ID/EX gets a bubble. Hold both fields during an older dmem wait or divide wait, and re\n…[36927 of 39999 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7a177c96c79ed761]…\nted instruction and define the registered replay training record.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Capture the prediction metadata with its instruction and preserve it across ID holds.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register successor repair and training on surviving EX advances and suppress younger forwarding, memory, and divider effects during repair.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the replay training collector and repair path while preserving the single-channel RVFI interface and architectural PC reporting.'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': \"Qualify load-use with the queued decode word's validity and preserve divide and dmem backpressure.\"}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check a short-tag alias, a changed source word, replay during imem stalls, EX repair priority over a pending guess, FENCE.I invalidation, and divide immediately after a cold redirect. Verify exact retirement order, PCs, and accepted data transactions.'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
