{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(l)\n if 'r11s1' in r['id'] or 'r10s1' in r['id']:\n  print(r['id'],json.dumps({k:r[k] for k in ('motivation','hypothesis','changes')},indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-002-r10s1 {\n  \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 270.74 CoreMark iterations/s at 101.544 MHz\\nand 3,750,582 marker cycles. The canonical stalled retirement trace\\ncontains 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions immediately after a load whose\\nnonzero destination they read. They occupy a load-use bubble today.\\nA direct data-RAM-to-EX comparator saved 129,454 marker cycles in a\\nscratch run, but the added RAM-to-repair path limited median Gowin\\nFmax to 65.652 MHz. Resolving these branches from registered load\\ndata can recover the issue slots while preserving a register boundary\\nat the memory response.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 270.74 CoreMark iterations/s at 101.544 MHz\\nand 3,750,582 marker cycles. The canonical stalled retirement trace\\ncontains 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions immediately after a load whose\\nnonzero destination they read. They occupy a load-use bubble today.\\nA direct data-RAM-to-EX comparator saved 129,454 marker cycles in a\\nscratch run, but the added RAM-to-repair path limited median Gowin\\nFmax to 65.652 MHz. Resolving these branches from registered load\\ndata can recover the issue slots while preserving a register boundary\\nat the memory response.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Classify a legal BEQ or BNE using the destination of the current\\nvalid EX load as a deferred branch. Register the two source matches\\nin ID/EX and admit the branch without the normal load-use bubble.\\nKeep that bubble for other consumers. Let the branch enter EX/MEM\\non the same edge that the load transfers its response to MEM/WB.\\nA data stall holds both instructions and their operand selections.\\nEX computes the direct and fall-through PC pairs and captures the\\nforwarded non-load operand. Save the equality of the ordinary\\nforwarded operands as a fallback when the preceding load traps.\\n\\nCompare the saved operand against the registered, extended load\\nword while the branch occupies EX/MEM and the next instruction can\\nexecute. Both source matches imply equality. Use the \n…[13012 of 16084 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bd0314052c3636bf]…\ncore.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Wire pair eligibility, the two memory comparison predicates and the extended load value used for RVFI.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Compare raw byte lanes against the registered source default and produce two masked group predicates in parallel with load formatting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Register the two comparison groups, two prequalified repair enables and correction PC. Use the same encoding for ordinary conditional branches and supported load pairs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Apply the repair token at the request mux and FIFO state boundary, including clear and retry when imem is stalled.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Exercise pair eligibility and fallback, signed and unsigned load widths, both matches, trapping loads, held data responses, taken and untaken repairs and exact ordered RVFI.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat bench/programs/Makefile && command -v verilator && command -v riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc && command -v gw_sh && ls -la /srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/968d1bd9'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat bench/programs/Makefile && command -v verilator && command -v riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc && command -v gw_sh && ls -la /srv/hwebench/tmp/5a1ea1b1/968d1bd9'","aggregated_output":"CROSS   := riscv32-unknown-elf\nCC      := $(CROSS)-gcc\n\n# CoreMark build knobs. Defaults are the canonical EEMBC reporting config\n# (2K data size, -O3); tools/eval/fpga.py's COREMARK_EXPECTED CRCs assume\n# exactly these defaults.\n# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\n#   the EEMBC canonical reporting config (used by VexRiscv et al.); 6000\n#   makes the matrix/list/state working sets ~3x larger so the score is\n#   harder to inflate via register-resident working sets.\n# - COREMARK_OPT: gcc optimization. -O3 is the standard CoreMark publication\n#   flag; -O2 is what the V0 baseline used.\n# Defaults match VexRiscv's published CoreMark methodology so the\n# orchestrator's fitness number is directly comparable to public CoreMark\n# results. To override (e.g. for the prior 6K -O2 V0 baseline):\n#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nCOREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000\nCOREMARK_OPT  ?= -O3\n\nCFLAGS  := -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 $(COREMARK_OPT) -static -nostartfiles \\\n           -specs=nano.specs -specs=nosys.specs \\\n           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\n           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\n           -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=$(COREMARK_SIZE)\n\nSRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_matrix.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_state.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_util.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.c \\\n        bench/programs/crt0.S\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: $(SRCS)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $^ -o $@\n\nbench/programs/selftest.elf: bench/programs/selftest.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n# Random full-trace programs (V2). The .S files are generated once by\n# gen_random_trace.py <seed> and committed, so every candidate runs the\n# same programs.\nRANDOM_ELFS := bench/programs/random1.elf bench/programs/random2.elf bench/programs/random3.elf\n\nbench/programs/random%.elf: bench/programs/random%.S\n\t$(CC) -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 -static -nostartfiles \\\n\t  -T bench/programs/link.ld $< -o $@\n\n.PHONY: all clean\nall: bench/programs/coremark.elf bench/programs/selftest.elf $(RANDOM_ELFS)\nclean:\n\trm -f bench/programs/*.elf\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/verilator\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
