{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'trace|marker|istall|dstall|usage' test/cosim/main.cpp | head -95; cat test/cosim/build.sh; ls -la /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/bench/programs | head -25; cat cores/bench/core.yaml; rg -n 'load_use|pipeline' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | head -25\"", "aggregated_output": "27:static bool oob_access = false;  // sticky: once set, final marker reports it\n32:// Benchmark-time MMIO markers. CoreMark's portme.c writes to BENCH_START\n63:        std::cerr << \"usage: sim <elf> [maxcycles] [--bench] [--istall] [--dstall] [--seed N]\\n\";\n68:    // --istall: random ~22% imem-bus backpressure (VexRiscv-style).\n69:    // --dstall: same on dmem bus. The orchestrator's fitness eval\n74:    bool istall = false;\n75:    bool dstall = false;\n78:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--istall\") == 0) istall     = true;\n79:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--dstall\") == 0) dstall     = true;\n119:        top->io_imemReady = istall ? bus_accepts_main() : 1;\n120:        top->io_dmemReady = dstall ? bus_accepts_main() : 1;\n131:        //     allowed (markers); anything else outside dmem is OOB (handled\n152:            // BENCH_START/BENCH_STOP markers at 0x10000100 / 0x10000104: record\n253:        // Emit final record, plus an explicit completion marker. Consumers MUST\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Build the Verilator-based cosim binary that drives `core` against an ELF\n# program. Produces $OBJ_DIR/cosim_sim (default: test/cosim/obj_dir/cosim_sim).\n#\n# RTL_DIR (default: rtl/) is globbed dynamically (with core_pkg.sv forced\n# first because its compilation-unit-scope typedefs and localparams must be\n# visible before any module references them). Hypotheses are allowed to add,\n# rename, or delete files inside rtl/, so a hardcoded file list would\n# silently break restructuring hypotheses.\nset -euo pipefail\n\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")/../..\" && pwd)\"\nCOSIM_DIR=\"$REPO_ROOT/test/cosim\"\nif [ -z \"${RTL_DIR:-}\" ] || [ -z \"${OBJ_DIR:-}\" ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: test/cosim/build.sh requires RTL_DIR and OBJ_DIR env vars.\" >&2\n  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl OBJ_DIR=cores/v1/obj_dir bash test/cosim/build.sh\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\n# NRET picks which RVFI port set main.cpp expects on `core`.\n# 1 = single-issue (only `_0` ports); 2 = dual-channel (both `_0` and `_1`).\n# Default 2 preserves existing behavior\n…[1768 of 4840 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e4738e4c8dfd5822]…\nrwxrwx--x+  1 nobody nogroup  45912 Nov 20 20:39 random2.elf\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup 142438 Nov 20 20:39 random3.S\n-rwxrwx--x+  1 nobody nogroup  47056 Nov 20 20:39 random3.elf\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup   3684 Nov 20 20:39 selftest.S\n-rwxrwx--x+  1 nobody nogroup   5248 Nov 20 20:39 selftest.elf\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 101.544\n  lut4: 6745\n  ff: 2410\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261121-003-r9s2\n  updated: '2026-11-21T02:36:41.819554Z'\n1:\"\"\"End-to-end pipeline tests for rtl/core.sv.\n373:async def load_use_stalls(dut, stall_cycles):\n962:def test_pipeline_runner():\n973:        test_module=\"test_pipeline\",\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
