{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys\nfor s in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(s); print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"title\\\"],d[\\\"outcome\\\"],d.get(\\\"cycles\\\"),d.get(\\\"fmax_mhz\\\")); print(d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"]); print(d.get(\\\"error\\\") or \\\"\\\")'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r1s1 Move DIV and REM into a clocked radix-4 unit improvement 4491485 45.918\n{'motivation': 'The baseline Gowin run reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU, with a median Fmax of 5.442 MHz. The ALU contains combinational signed and unsigned division and remainder whose outputs pass through the integer result mux. The divider is the leading candidate for the path depth, so splitting it across clocks could shorten the period for every instruction. A baseline Verilator trace with both bus stalls enabled matched the logged 4,491,485 marker-to-marker cycles and passed UART/CRC validation. It retired 93,960 MUL instructions and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions inside those markers, making the divider a candidate for extra latency with no direct cycle cost in the measured workload.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Move DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU into one blocking, clocked radix-4 divider on the EX result path. Capture the forwarded source values and unsigned magnitudes at issue, then register the divisor thresholds D, 2D and 3D. Zero-pad the dividend to 36 bits and process three radix-4 digits per clock for six clocks, registering the quotient and partial remainder between groups. Each digit compares the 34-bit trial remainder with the thresholds using three parallel 35-bit subtractions, then selects the highest digit whose subtraction did not borrow. Correct the sign of the selected quotient or remainder on the EX/MEM transfer edge. Carry the original operands and mode for RVFI and for the RV32M divide-by-zero and signed-overflow results. Use the same bounded issue, wait and completion schedule for the existing ALTOPS formulas so the 20-step checks continue to exercise divider stalls, forwarding and retirement. An eight-cycle launch-to-EX/MEM interval fits the ten-cycle liveness window even with a preceding load-use or redirect bubble on the zero-wait formal buses.\\n\\nHold the divide in ID/EX and stop fetch while it runs. Let older instructions drain in order, preserve any unaccept\n…[61579 of 64651 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a0272a237442a842]…\nd\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: finished (returncode=1)\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] engine_0: Status returned by engine: FAIL\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:36 (96)\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:36 (96)\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned FAIL\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary: counterexample trace: pc_fwd_ch0/engine_0/trace.vcd\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] summary:   failed assertion rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__assert_rvfi_pc_fwd_check_sv_41_61 at rvfi_pc_fwd_check.sv:41.6-41.69 step 20\nSBY  8:45:48 [pc_fwd_ch0] DONE (FAIL, rc=0)\n\nFull run log: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-002-r12s1/formal/last_run-h5794090eee034aa.log\nPer-check logs in: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep3/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-002-r12s1/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-h5794090eee034aa/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
