{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_15", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"jq -rc 'select(.id==\\\"hyp-20261121-002-r12s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261121-001-r12s0\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261121-002-r7s1\\\" or .id==\\\"hyp-20261121-002-r8s1\\\") | {id, outcome, cycles, fmax_mhz, critical_path, seeds, error, hypothesis}' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\":\"hyp-20261121-002-r7s1\",\"outcome\":\"regression\",\"cycles\":4148503,\"fmax_mhz\":97.608,\"critical_path\":{\"from\":\"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_data_29_s0\",\"to\":\"cpu/u_if/use_redirect_pc_q_s0\",\"slack_ns\":-5.763,\"arrival_ns\":16.057,\"logic_cells\":11,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_if\"]},\"seeds\":[92.912,97.608,97.608],\"error\":null,\"hypothesis\":{\"motivation\":\"The bench champion scores 231.39 CoreMark iter/s over 4,148,503 marker\\ncycles at a 95.991 MHz Gowin median. Its median-setting placements report\\na forwarded-operand path into the shared integer result register, with\\na product-to-branch path close behind. Round 6 eliminated a mux before\\nthe raw result lanes, but each operand still selects separate ADD, SUB,\\nand two product words. The stalled champion trace contains 93,960 MUL\\nretirements, including 35,640 with a dependent next instruction.\\nAll multiplies inside the markers return the low word.\\n\",\"hypothesis\":\"Narrow the single-cycle EX/MEM bypass to one ADD/SUB word, one shared\\ninteger and special word, and one low multiply word. Compute MUL with\\na dedicated 32-bit product in EX. Capture the forwarded operands and\\nsign bits for MULH, MULHSU, and MULHU at EX/MEM and compute their high\\nword in MEM. Forward those high results from MEM/WB, with a one-cycle\\ninterlock for an adjacent consumer that actually reads a matching\\nnonzero destination. Independent successors continue to issue.\\nThis removes two word inputs from each EX operand mux and preserves\\nimmediate low-word multiply forwarding. Preserve exact ALTOPS\\nsubstitutions at the same stage boundaries as the hardware results.\\nDecode the bitwise, compare, and shift operation enables before ID/EX.\\nUse those registered enables to select the shared integer result in\\nparallel with the link, AUIPC, and divide terms. This preserves a single\\nbypass word for that lane and removes operation decode from its EX path.\\n\\nA scratch implementation passed stalled CoreMark with canonical CRCs\\nat 4,148,503 marker cycles and matched the ISS on selftest and all t\n…[20225 of 23297 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:381c07df90c6e144]…\nwarding selections for trap fallback.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/hazard_unit.sv\",\"description\":\"Admit eligible pairs without the load-use bubble and preserve repair priority and data-request holds.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/core.sv\",\"description\":\"Connect the IF/ID buffer, wire memory completion and eligible pairs across the existing boundaries and retain the ordered replay training handoff.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Supply raw load response and eligible completion, produce grouped byte and extension predicates, and preserve accepted-access and trap behavior.\"},{\"file\":\"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\"description\":\"Capture the exact dependent address or comparison groups at EX/MEM and carry the resolved operands to RVFI. Select the ordinary execution path if the older load traps.\"},{\"file\":\"test/test_pipeline.py\",\"description\":\"Check back-to-back dependent loads at both displacements, address carry and wraparound, misalignment of either access, stalls, load-fed equality branches, and exact channel-0 traces through repair.\"}]}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
