{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261121-(002-r14s1|002-r13s1|001-r14s0|003-r13s2)\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; keys=\\\"id motivation hypothesis fitness fmax_mhz cycles lut4 ff dsp critical_path implementation_notes\\\".split(); [print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"{k}: {o.get(k)}\\\" for k in keys)+\\\"\\\\n\\\") for l in sys.stdin for o in [json.loads(l)]]'\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-002-r13s1\nmotivation: The champion runs canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,750,582 marker cycles\nat 101.544 MHz. Profiling that run counted 133,940 load-use bubbles on\nequality branches and 58,947 on loads. Round 12 recovered 185,459 cycles\nwith both response consumers and scored 277.47 iterations/s at 98.923 MHz.\nIts median placements were limited by JALR correction into fetch.\nSeparate the address captured for the next dmem request from the PC\nand successor captured for repair so a load pair adds no address\nselection or increment to the repair cycle.\n\nhypothesis: {'motivation': 'The champion runs canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,750,582 marker cycles\\nat 101.544 MHz. Profiling that run counted 133,940 load-use bubbles on\\nequality branches and 58,947 on loads. Round 12 recovered 185,459 cycles\\nwith both response consumers and scored 277.47 iterations/s at 98.923 MHz.\\nIts median placements were limited by JALR correction into fetch.\\nSeparate the address captured for the next dmem request from the PC\\nand successor captured for repair so a load pair adds no address\\nselection or increment to the repair cycle.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"At the existing EX/MEM boundary, capture the next memory request and\\na separate fetch correction PC pair. For a legal load whose rs1 matches\\nthe nonzero destination of the immediately older LW, admit offsets\\n0, 1, and 2. Present its full byte address on the cycle after the older\\nrequest completes. Form the candidate from the raw response using\\nparallel prefix carries for the short displacement. Select the\\nordinary rs1-plus-immediate fallback when the producer traps. Make\\nthis selection before the dmem address register, since a scratch\\nlayout with address arithmetic after the register lost Gowin block RAM\\ninference in the unchanged wrapper.\\n\\nPredecode the two pair kinds when filling the bus and replay lanes.\\nMove the corresponding bits into the issue register with the exact\\ninstruction they describe. In ID, match true load destinations and\\nuse the registered ol\n…[24489 of 27561 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f677cd7bda308a78]…\nc instruction just outside the instruction window incorrectly reported the preceding load's result as both x0 operands. IF now captures the zero instruction with cleared metadata outside the window, and a directed test covers this case. An intermediate split-writeback revision completed 11 of 53 formal checks with no new counterexample reported. The unchanged single-issue formal suite was started on the retained RTL after selecting it from the completed timings, and it remained incomplete at handoff.\n- Verilator lint, all six cocotb runners, and cosim for selftest, the three random traces, and CoreMark passed. Canonical CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 3,589,985 marker cycles with the expected CRCs and validation message.\n- Gowin placements 0, 1 and 2 reached 99.794, 105.016 and 105.016 MHz. The median yields 292.52 iterations per second, 2.2% above the supplied champion and below the fitness target. The median setup path crosses the divider's wide-remainder logic, whose schedule and RTL were preserved.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
