{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; rows=[json.loads(line) for line in sys.stdin]; print(\\\"fields\\\",sorted(rows[-1])); [print(\\\"\\\\n\\\", {k:v for k,v in r.items() if k not in (\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"eval\\\",\\\"result\\\",\\\"results\\\")}, \\\"\\\\n\\\",r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\")) for r in rows]'\"", "aggregated_output": "fields ['bsram', 'category', 'changes', 'cosim_passed', 'critical_path', 'cycles', 'delta_pct', 'dsp', 'error', 'expected_impact', 'ff', 'fitness', 'fmax_mhz', 'formal_passed', 'hypothesis', 'id', 'implementation_notes', 'ipc_coremark', 'iterations', 'lesson', 'logic_levels', 'lut4', 'lutram', 'motivation', 'outcome', 'perturbations', 'round_id', 'seeds', 'slot', 'timestamp', 'title', 'vs_baseline']\n\n {'id': 'hyp-20261120-002-r1s1', 'title': 'Move DIV and REM into a clocked radix-4 unit', 'category': 'structural', 'motivation': 'The baseline Gowin run reports a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through forwarding and the EX ALU, with a median Fmax of 5.442 MHz. The ALU contains combinational signed and unsigned division and remainder whose outputs pass through the integer result mux. The divider is the leading candidate for the path depth, so splitting it across clocks could shorten the period for every instruction. A baseline Verilator trace with both bus stalls enabled matched the logged 4,491,485 marker-to-marker cycles and passed UART/CRC validation. It retired 93,960 MUL instructions and zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU instructions inside those markers, making the divider a candidate for extra latency with no direct cycle cost in the measured workload.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 50, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/div_unit.sv', 'description': 'Add the shared radix-4 recurrence, registered operands and divisor multiples, bounded control, signed correction and RV32M corner cases. Keep result and source metadata stable until consumed. Register the equivalent ALTOPS result at issue and present it on the same completion schedule.'}, {'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Remove the DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU combinational arms and move their ALTOPS formulas to the divider. Preserve the base-ISA and MUL-family result paths.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Launch a valid divide once with the forwarded operands when the older EX/MEM entry can advance. Insert EX/MEM bubbles during\n…[35028 of 38100 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4a205982f99a3025]…\n53 single-retire ALTOPS checks on the first attempt with the final RTL. The real M-extension arithmetic was exercised by cocotb and ISS co-simulation.\n- Verilator lint completed without warnings. All six cocotb runners passed. The suite covers adjacent ADD, SUB, integer, and special results, all four multiply variants, youngest-writer priority, fallback after trapping JALR and load instructions, and forwarding through five-cycle data stalls. Divider vectors include all 255 nonzero narrow divisor magnitudes and exact multiples that exercise quotient correction.\n- Co-simulation matched the ISS on selftest and all three random programs with zero-wait and stalled buses. CoreMark validated the canonical CRCs over 4,148,503 stalled marker cycles for 10 iterations.\n- Gowin reported 89.707, 95.991, and 95.991 MHz. The median of 95.991 MHz yields 231.39 CoreMark iterations/s, 16.11% above the supplied champion. Placement option 0 used 4,429 logic cells, 1,318 registers, 32 LUT RAMs, 5 BSRAM blocks, and 4 DSP blocks.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
