{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'GOWIN|gw_sh|tmp|BUILD_DIR|timing' tools/eval/gowin.py Makefile | head -100; command -v gw_sh; ls /opt; command -v verilator; command -v riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc; cat formal/checks_si.cfg\"","aggregated_output":"Makefile:1:.PHONY: help lint test test-infra cosim formal fpga timing next loop report bench clean\nMakefile:83:\t@echo \"  make timing TARGET=v1   — Gowin Fmax and worst paths (placement option 0)\"\nMakefile:135:# FPGA timing and area come from the vendor flow, Gowin EDA\nMakefile:140:timing:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:1:\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\ntools/eval/gowin.py:4:route and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\ntools/eval/gowin.py:22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\ntools/eval/gowin.py:61:        \"set_option -gen_text_timing_rpt 1\",\ntools/eval/gowin.py:77:    modules the path crosses (in order), from Gowin's timing report.\"\"\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:114:        return {\"placement_failed\": True, \"fmax_mhz\": None, \"reason\": \"no Fmax in timing report\"}\ntools/eval/gowin.py:128:def _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:155:    # Plain threads and blocking waits, no asyncio: agents run `make timing`\ntools/eval/gowin.py:158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:200:    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\ntools/eval/gowin.py:214:                                wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\", options=opts)\ntools/eval/gowin.py:221:        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\ngowin\nhwe-python\nhwe-toolchain\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/verilator\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
