{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines():\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get(\\\"round_id\\\",0)>=6:\n  print(d.get('id'),d.get('fitness'),d.get('cycles'),d.get('seeds'),d.get('critical_path'))\n  for key in ['hypothesis','implementation_notes']:\n   print(key, str(d.get(key))[:6300])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r6s0 215.55 4037811 [79.799, 87.033, 87.033] {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.ex_mem_match_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_19_s0', 'slack_ns': -7.531, 'arrival_ns': 17.826, 'logic_cells': 11, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The current front end discards ready imem responses when a load-use interlock or an older dmem stall blocks decode. Two buffered sequential words can turn those otherwise idle fetch opportunities into instructions for later imem stall cycles. A fall-through path keeps the current fetch latency when the FIFO is empty.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Add a two-word fall-through FIFO in IF. Keep the existing PC banks as the address of the next instruction to issue. With zero, one, or two words queued, request that address, its successor, or the address two words ahead, respectively. Use the live imem response when the FIFO is empty and the head word otherwise. Enqueue a ready response when there is room and it did not issue by fall-through. Pop only when decode accepts the head, permit replacement on a simultaneous pop, and advance the issue PC exactly once per normal accepted instruction. A queued word is valid independently of live imem readiness. The hazard check must see the instruction offered to ID and keep the existing load-use interlock. A dmem stall still holds ID/EX and both older stages while IF can fill the FIFO.\\n\\nPredecode one possible-transfer bit from the live imem opcode for B, JAL, or JALR. Store that bit with each queued word and select it using head validity, in parallel with instruction selection. Clear both FIFO valid bits when decode accepts a word with this bit set. Block refill while a valid branch or jump occupies EX. The FIFO is then empty when a redirect resolves, so redirect logic only selects the imem address, the existing PC metadata, and the registered redirect bank. Update the sequential bank independently of the branch predicate. Preserve the same-cycle B/JAL target fetch and retry, the JALR squ\n…[39094 of 42166 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:836431acc8953901]…\ng implementation.\n\nThe pipeline tests cover replay during imem stalls, refill during a held dmem request, counter updates, stale JALR target repair, suppression of wrong-path stores and divider issues, FENCE.I with self-modifying code, and instruction-window and alignment cases. The harness checks full retirement order and PC sequences and continues to assert held dmem request stability.\n\nVerilator lint, all six cocotb runners, and single-channel co-simulation passed. The pipeline runner passed all 32 scenarios. Canonical stalled CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 3,819,059 marker cycles, with all five expected CRCs, the validation message, and no out-of-bounds accesses.\n\nThe three Gowin placements reached 93.441, 95.128 and 95.128 MHz. The 95.128 MHz median gives 249.09 CoreMark iterations per second, above the 242.034 acceptance threshold. The option 0 critical path runs from a multiplier result to the registered direct-transfer selector. The other two placements are limited by the existing wide divider.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
