{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nins = ['hyp-20261121-003-r10s2','hyp-20261121-003-r11s2','hyp-20261121-003-r12s2','hyp-20261121-003-r13s2','hyp-20261121-002-r13s1']\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d.get('id') not in ins: continue\n print(d['id'], d.get('title'), d.get('cycles'), d.get('fmax_mhz'), sorted(d.keys()))\n print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n print(str(d.get('implementation_notes', ''))[:5000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-003-r10s2 Separate direct prediction from replay packet completion None None ['category', 'changes', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'expected_impact', 'formal_passed', 'hypothesis', 'id', 'motivation', 'outcome', 'round_id', 'slot', 'title']\nMake an accepted direct prediction independent of replay lane count.\nKeep 32 entries and train a tagged target-only entry when a legal,\naligned taken B/JAL has an in-window target and the collector stops\nbefore its first word. Its resume PC is the target itself. Encode\ninstallation eligibility separately from the last-lane mask so an\nempty fill and a counter-only update are distinct. Keep the two-bit\nconditional direction counter and strongly taken JAL state. Retain\nthe early short-tag forecast and following-cycle validation against\nthe full tag and exact fetched source instruction.\n\nA validated empty packet delivers predicted-taken to ID and releases\nits slot as soon as the source issues. A nonempty packet keeps its slot\nthrough the last replay word. Save validated steering and the lane mask\nseparately for queued slots. When a fresh guess is at the head, use\nthe sampled lane mask for the issue-word mux and the exact hit for\ncredit accounting. A failed validation keeps the source's PC+4 path\nand discards the younger speculative response. A simultaneous EX repair\nowns fetch and refills slot zero directly from imem_ready. Compute that\nrefill credit independently of normal push, pop, load-use, and divide\ncontrols. Clear younger ID/EX and suppress its forwarding and divider\nissue while the resolver remains held through the repair edge.\n\nPipeline the PC-relative adder that supplies the direct repair target.\nIn ID compute the low 15 word-address bits and carry for both PC+offset\nand PC+offset+1. In parallel compute the high 15 bits with carry-in\nzero and with carry-in one. Capture these partial sums with the decoded\nword on the normal ID/EX edge. EX selects each high half with its saved\ncarry and uses the assembled target and successor for repair. AUIPC\nuses the same assembl\n…[17431 of 20503 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f2949ef17ef7ce55]…\n terminal counter.\n\nPreserve ordinary decode, execution and EX repair for every replayed\nbranch and JAL. Form the architectural sequential PC by widening\nbefore incrementing the stored word PC. Repair discards younger\ntraces and preserves the resolver and its link. FENCE.I clears\ndescriptor validity, in-flight training and queued replay. Retain\nthe current trap, bus window and single-channel retirement contracts.\n\nA trace-driven model using the evaluator's stall sequence reproduced\nthe champion's marker count and estimates 3,647,865 cycles for this\norganization, 102,717 fewer than the champion. The model assumes\nuninterrupted one-word-per-cycle replay when ID is ready, including\ntrace entry and wrap. At that cycle count the acceptance floor of\n283.19 iterations/s requires a median above 103.31 MHz. A 105 MHz\nmedian would reach 287.84 iterations/s, up 6.3%. Measure replay\nbubbles, source and interior repairs, canonical stalled CoreMark,\nand all three Gowin placements, and run the existing correctness gates.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
