{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261121-003-r(10|13|14)s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; [(lambda d: print(d[\\\"id\\\"], d.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"), d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"), sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\"))(json.loads(l)) for l in sys.stdin]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-003-r10s2\n{'motivation': \"The bench champion scores 270.74 iterations/s at 101.544 MHz over\\n3,750,582 stalled CoreMark marker cycles. The predictor can install a\\ntaken entry only when it collects a replay word. This leaves a hot B\\nor JAL unpredicted when its target starts with another control transfer.\\nThe champion's marker window incurred 52,585 repairs to direct targets.\\nIts Gowin option 0 also reported a repair-to-FIFO-occupancy path.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Make an accepted direct prediction independent of replay lane count.\\nKeep 32 entries and train a tagged target-only entry when a legal,\\naligned taken B/JAL has an in-window target and the collector stops\\nbefore its first word. Its resume PC is the target itself. Encode\\ninstallation eligibility separately from the last-lane mask so an\\nempty fill and a counter-only update are distinct. Keep the two-bit\\nconditional direction counter and strongly taken JAL state. Retain\\nthe early short-tag forecast and following-cycle validation against\\nthe full tag and exact fetched source instruction.\\n\\nA validated empty packet delivers predicted-taken to ID and releases\\nits slot as soon as the source issues. A nonempty packet keeps its slot\\nthrough the last replay word. Save validated steering and the lane mask\\nseparately for queued slots. When a fresh guess is at the head, use\\nthe sampled lane mask for the issue-word mux and the exact hit for\\ncredit accounting. A failed validation keeps the source's PC+4 path\\nand discards the younger speculative response. A simultaneous EX repair\\nowns fetch and refills slot zero directly from imem_ready. Compute that\\nrefill credit independently of normal push, pop, load-use, and divide\\ncontrols. Clear younger ID/EX and suppress its forwarding and divider\\nissue while the resolver remains held through the repair edge.\\n\\nPipeline the PC-relative adder that supplies the direct repair target.\\nIn ID compute the low 15 word-address bits and carry for both PC+offset\\nand PC+offset+1. In parallel compute the high 1\n…[16351 of 19423 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6e0149dd1bec0d59]…\nCE.I, and full-width links at the instruction-window boundary.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint, all six cocotb runners, and single-channel co-simulation passed. Co-simulation covered selftest, three random traces, and CoreMark. The canonical stalled CoreMark run completed 10 iterations in 3,414,350 marker cycles, 150,518 fewer than the champion. The UART banner and all five canonical CRCs matched, with `oob=false`.\n- The local `formal/run_all.sh` run used the single-channel wrapper. Causality, illegal instruction, backward PC, liveness, and unique order passed. The run was stopped at the local time limit with the other 48 checks incomplete and no reported counterexample.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 93.550, 96.111, and 96.111 MHz. The median corresponds to 281.49 iterations/s and missed the 103 MHz target. Option 0 used 7,901 LUT4, 2,768 registers, and 17 block RAMs. The worst paths run from the source-instruction block RAM through exact validation to the fetch occupancy register.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
