{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r15s2.yaml && git status --short --untracked-files=all'", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-003-r15s2\ntitle: Read replay source identity one fetch ahead\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  Eight-word conditional successor replay in r14s2 saved 150,518 stalled\n  CoreMark marker cycles, but its median dropped to 96.111 MHz. The timed\n  path ran from the source-instruction block RAM through exact validation\n  to IF FIFO occupancy. At 3,414,350 cycles, the 286.24 iter/s champion's\n  4.6% acceptance margin requires a median above 102.228 MHz. Shortening\n  this path could preserve the largest measured predictor cycle savings.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use the 128-row hashed predictor with one sequential packet of up to\n  eight words for the currently favored successor of each source. Hash\n  the in-window source PC with PC[8:2] XOR PC[15:9]. Read two copies of\n  the synchronous source-identity table one fetch ahead. One read uses\n  the next sequential or held cursor's index. The other uses the current\n  source descriptor's saved resume index. Compute those addresses in\n  parallel with the short-tag forecast so its direction decision stays\n  off the block RAM address paths. Keep the sequential successor index\n  beside the cursor and save the resume successor's index at publication.\n  This keeps cursor selection out of the increment-and-hash path. Store the exact instruction and\n  PC[19:9] in each identity copy. The hash and retained tag identify every\n  aligned PC in the window.\n\n  At the edge accepting the source bus word, compare the instruction in\n  byte groups and the full remaining tag against the prefetched records.\n  Register the group matches and use the selected cursor's registered\n  matches to validate the guess on the next cycle. The identity read and\n  comparison now complete an