only legal, trap-free conditional branches when valid EX\nadvances. Register update-valid, index, and outcome before a separate\ntraining read and saturating write. Reset the entry-valid bitmap and\npending update valid. On an untrained index, predict backward taken\nand forward not taken, then initialize weakly toward the first resolved\noutcome. A fetch on a table write edge samples the pre-edge state.\nHold the PC and ID/EX on older dmem backpressure or a divider wait.\nAdvance speculatively only on an acc\n…[6638 of 9710 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a116fd9f7a862179]…\nt bus readiness.\n\nCompare only the predicted and actual aligned direct directions in EX.\nRegister a repair valid bit and the full resolved target or fall-through\non EX advance. Use registered repair for aligned JALR as well. In the\nrepair cycle discard the younger FIFO contents and annul the younger\nID/EX instruction before it can issue a divide, train the predictor, or\nenter EX/MEM as a producer or memory operation. Offer the registered\ncorrection directly to imem and ID in that cycle, overriding FIFO\nfullness. Save the corrected address\nfor retry if imem stalls. Derive RVFI next PC, traps and links from actual\nEX resolution, including misaligned and cross-region transfers.\n\nAt the scratch cycle count, the acceptance cutoff of 208.46 iter/s\nrequires median Fmax above 82.97 MHz. Keep the window guard on acceptance\nand the external address, and keep the registered repair and the guard\noff the queue payload computation. Check the full formal gate and all\nthree Gowin placements after integrating the predictor.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
