{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261121-003-r8s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json; r=json.load(sys.stdin); print(r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"]); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"", "aggregated_output": "\nExtend branch target prediction to replay up to six consecutive words\nat a hot direct target. Use a 64-entry direct-mapped table indexed by\nsource PC[7:2] with its full in-window tag and exact B/JAL kind and\ndisplacement. Only a legal, matching fetched B/JAL can use an entry.\nPredict JAL taken and learn conditional directions with two-bit\nsaturating counters. Store the target word PC, replay length, and\nprecomputed PC after the prefix so the fetch cursor can skip the cached\nwords. Store each word in its own unreset, flat distributed RAM lane\nand reset the validity and counter training state. Limit packets and\ntheir resume PCs to the instruction window. On a miss, fetch normally\nand predict fall-through. Aligned JALR continues through resolved repair.\n\nOn a ready imem response, enqueue the fetched instruction and its\noptional target prefix in a four-packet queue, including the active\npacket. Store the fetched word and each prefix word in independent\nflat lanes. Shift the active packet on an ID acceptance so a fixed\nword register drives ID. On its last acceptance, load the next packet\ninto the active registers on the same edge. With no waiting packet,\nload a simultaneous enqueue directly into the active registers when\nempty or when the last word issues. Supply the source PC for\nthe transfer and the target PC and successive word addresses for\nreplayed instructions. Each replayed word has a sequential successor.\nContinue filling free slots while ID is held by load-use, divide, or\ndmem backpressure. Use registered occupancy and keep inert payload\nwrites separate from the execute repair decision. Request the first\nuncached word while the prefix issues.\n\nTrain from the ordered stream of valid, surviving EX/MEM advances.\nRegister the source signature, resolved target and aligned taken flag\nwith the direct transfer. Start collecting when the next surviving\ninstruction's PC equals that target,\nand append consecutive in-window words until six have been collected.\nStop before every control-flow or fence opcode, or at any di\n…[1092 of 4164 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:22c71e4b38c94546]…\nedge\nand suppress its retirement during that hold. Release it on the next\nedge even if imem was stalled, so an immediate divide can overlap the\nrepair refill without violating the formal liveness bound. Preserve\nfull architectural successors and traps, keep bus addresses in bounds,\nand retain the nret=1 contract and existing correctness gates.\n\nA trace-driven cycle model with 64 entries, six-word prefixes, four\npacket slots and the evaluator stall stream estimated 3,735,628\nmarker cycles, 291,865 replay hits and 1,031,702 replayed words.\nIts two-slot configuration estimated 3,884,536 cycles. The model\nblocks wrong-path fetch after a miss and resumes from the correction\non the repair edge. At 3,735,628 cycles the acceptance floor of\n262.57 iter/s requires over 98.09 MHz median. Target 100.5 MHz,\nabout 269 iter/s. Measure this version in RTL with all three Gowin\nplacements. Check cold misses, direction reversals, nested transfers,\nload and divide holds, aliases, FENCE.I, and a divide immediately\nafter repair.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
